WEBVTT

1
00:01:52.988 --> 00:01:54.698
We'll see who uses a bulb now!

2
00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.246
Welcome one...

3
00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:04.041
Welcome all...

4
00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:06.460
Here's Sitabo...

5
00:02:06.752 --> 00:02:08.962
And this one's Gulabo...

6
00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:12.859
She comes with a 'Hazratganj' tag.

7
00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:17.113
And this one's landed from 'Aminabad,
Gadbadjhala'...

8
00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.857
And all she wants is to lose herself
in the lanes of 'Chandni Chowk'.

9
00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.784
Smart is she.

10
00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.369
And clever is she.

11
00:02:23.393 --> 00:02:27.415
The battle is set,
The lines are drawn, Seething in anger,

12
00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:30.585
Gulabo fights,
Oh yeah, Sitabo fights.

13
00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:37.449
When the village gathered for a feast...

14
00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:01.223
- Here you go.
- Hmm.

15
00:03:02.224 --> 00:03:03.826
- Begum!
- Yes?

16
00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.994
Check these out once... Will you?

17
00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.269
Wait a bit, mister.

18
00:03:15.821 --> 00:03:19.759
The battle is set, The lines are drawn,
Seething in anger,

19
00:03:19.783 --> 00:03:22.678
Gulabo fights,
Oh yeah, Sitabo fights.

20
00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:26.099
The battle is set, The lines are drawn,
Seething in anger,

21
00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:29.102
Gulabo fights,
Oh yeah, Sitabo fights.

22
00:03:29.126 --> 00:03:32.563
The battle is set, The lines are drawn,
Seething in anger,

23
00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:37.485
Payal... Neetu...
Gulabo fights, Oh yeah, Sitabo fights.

24
00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:41.614
Payal... Neetu... The battle is set,
The lines are drawn, Seething in anger,

25
00:03:41.638 --> 00:03:45.100
What on earth is going on?

26
00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:49.604
I've been around the
whole town looking for you two...

27
00:03:49.855 --> 00:03:51.332
...and here you are,
embarrassing the family name!

28
00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:53.000
C'mmon missies,
out of here for shame sake.

29
00:03:53.024 --> 00:03:56.295
And you, Mirza,
only a douche bag like you would...

30
00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:59.298
...make my little girls dance
on the streets. I swear if you ever...

31
00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:01.801
There you go again, with your tongue...

32
00:04:01.825 --> 00:04:04.637
...moving faster than
a pickpocket's scissors.

33
00:04:04.661 --> 00:04:08.182
Now if I start using mine,
you wouldn't know where to run.

34
00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:12.019
Spare me your nonsense
and give me my share of pennies.

35
00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:14.397
- Oh forget it, he's the greediest man alive.
- Hah...! Never.

36
00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:16.399
Yeah am fine being greedy.

37
00:04:16.423 --> 00:04:18.484
Ya what more can an old sourpuss be.

38
00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:24.991
I'll eat milk pudding with
saffron extracts and won't share.

39
00:04:25.015 --> 00:04:26.224
Greedy, yeah.

40
00:04:26.892 --> 00:04:28.310
Go to hell!

41
00:04:43.158 --> 00:04:44.993
Twenty rupees...

42
00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:19.528
Stop dropping it on my forehead!

43
00:05:20.362 --> 00:05:25.051
Well I'm not doing it on purpose...
sit straight then, will you?

44
00:05:25.075 --> 00:05:28.787
Get off from here...

45
00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:32.582
Don't you stain my face!

46
00:05:32.958 --> 00:05:34.977
Now who's lit this
bulb early in the morning?

47
00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.295
Switch it off!

48
00:05:38.463 --> 00:05:43.009
Mumbling...

49
00:05:45.053 --> 00:05:47.573
- Tch... what're you doing, Begum?
- I'm just wiping-

50
00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:50.076
This'll dry up in no time.
It's April for god sake!

51
00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.787
-And when did April come?

52
00:05:52.811 --> 00:05:55.706
How the hell does it matter?

53
00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:59.317
Payal, set up Dadda's tiffin.

54
00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:06.634
Amongst all these things... that huge bucket...
those leather chappals... goats...

55
00:06:06.658 --> 00:06:08.994
...all that got stolen was my damn bulb?

56
00:06:09.661 --> 00:06:11.472
His bicycle bell is missing too.

57
00:06:11.496 --> 00:06:12.723
To hell with your bell!

58
00:06:12.747 --> 00:06:18.980
- My bell!
- Oh just ignore this gobshite and get me some tea.

59
00:06:19.004 --> 00:06:21.732
My bulb got stolen and
you're calling me names? Really?

60
00:06:21.756 --> 00:06:25.987
He's crying as if he's lost
all his goddamn family wealth.

61
00:06:26.011 --> 00:06:29.014
He doesn't even have
a face of a wealthy man!

62
00:06:29.556 --> 00:06:32.159
Remember the day Nehru ji came,

63
00:06:32.183 --> 00:06:36.038
those petty thieves were all
over the town plaguing it like rats...

64
00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:40.459
...must be one of them who stole his bulb.

65
00:06:40.483 --> 00:06:41.651
Bang on, Begum!

66
00:06:42.193 --> 00:06:44.672
He's a plagued rat of a thief
who's been stealing off us...

67
00:06:44.696 --> 00:06:46.990
...and making a measly penny or two.

68
00:06:47.866 --> 00:06:50.076
Well he better watch out
'cause I won't spare him.

69
00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:08.988
Why are you forever stuck to the TV?

70
00:07:09.012 --> 00:07:10.013
Go study.

71
00:07:10.513 --> 00:07:13.099
I'm done with my home work...
moreover, it's a holiday.

72
00:07:13.808 --> 00:07:15.852
So? All the more reason to study... uh...

73
00:07:16.645 --> 00:07:17.663
What grade are you in?

74
00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:18.813
Three.

75
00:07:19.981 --> 00:07:23.026
Three? But I've been paying
that damn fee for years!

76
00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.212
Brother!

77
00:07:25.236 --> 00:07:26.236
What?

78
00:07:27.197 --> 00:07:28.382
I want to take up a job.

79
00:07:28.406 --> 00:07:29.949
Get done with your grade 12 first.

80
00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:32.432
I'm in the final year of undergrads.

81
00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.999
I'd told her to let you know.

82
00:07:41.002 --> 00:07:41.938
What grade are you in?

83
00:07:41.962 --> 00:07:43.046
Eighth.

84
00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:47.092
C'mmon you guys are not
allowed to grow up that fast!

85
00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:50.655
Your brother is not a rich dude yet.

86
00:07:50.679 --> 00:07:52.698
So there's no point talking to him!

87
00:07:52.722 --> 00:07:55.034
As for me, marriage is not my thing...

88
00:07:55.058 --> 00:07:57.620
I'd much rather earn my own salary
and live respectfully...

89
00:07:57.644 --> 00:07:59.664
...in any case,
I'm living in this home of ours.

90
00:07:59.688 --> 00:08:02.065
Yeah but we don't own it...
it's a rented one.

91
00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:05.860
Rent? We've grabbed it!

92
00:08:09.531 --> 00:08:11.157
What rubbish!

93
00:08:11.741 --> 00:08:14.744
That's what Uncle Mirza
goes around saying it to everyone.

94
00:08:16.037 --> 00:08:18.206
Mirza needs to be dug up
in this mansion.

95
00:08:20.709 --> 00:08:22.919
Are you nuts?!

96
00:08:40.854 --> 00:08:47.652
Your tenant Baankey Rastogi,
he's a daft pillock!

97
00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:52.741
Do you really reckon that he, an owner
of a wheat mill in the main market...

98
00:08:53.074 --> 00:08:54.993
...won't have money to pay a higher rent?

99
00:08:56.036 --> 00:08:59.456
Are you asking me this or telling me?

100
00:08:59.789 --> 00:09:01.976
Umm... no I am just saying.

101
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.543
Oh ok, just saying.

102
00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:08.131
That where on earth can one rent
out a house for just 30 rupees?

103
00:09:08.715 --> 00:09:10.693
You won't stop grating on my nerves,
will you?

104
00:09:10.717 --> 00:09:12.903
And only if you were less thick...

105
00:09:12.927 --> 00:09:15.208
...you'd remember
he hasn't paid up for last three months.

106
00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:17.974
Of course I know his story.

107
00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:20.769
His aunt died, father died.

108
00:09:21.519 --> 00:09:24.355
He's still stuck around
like a blood-sucking leech.

109
00:09:25.148 --> 00:09:27.567
The day Begum dies...

110
00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:31.529
...I swear to her grave, I am going
to throw out these roaches of tenants...

111
00:09:31.905 --> 00:09:36.427
...who are infesting my home
and then that mansion...

112
00:09:36.451 --> 00:09:37.744
It'll be yours...

113
00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:43.166
Yeah... only mine.

114
00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:50.590
Say that again...

115
00:09:50.924 --> 00:09:53.218
Mansion will be yours!

116
00:09:54.803 --> 00:09:56.513
Mansion will be mine!

117
00:10:11.778 --> 00:10:14.906
There are five of us
staying in a pigeonhole, Fauzia...

118
00:10:16.908 --> 00:10:20.912
...a small curtained section in the kitchen
is where my mom and sisters bathe...

119
00:10:21.746 --> 00:10:25.041
...and we share the toilet
with Mishraji's family...

120
00:10:28.211 --> 00:10:31.357
...how do I even think of getting married?

121
00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:33.591
When did I even ask for marriage?

122
00:10:34.592 --> 00:10:36.928
But I didn't know you were this poor...

123
00:10:38.304 --> 00:10:40.390
I mean, I thought
staying in FATIMA MAHAL...

124
00:10:40.765 --> 00:10:42.076
...you must be of some rich lineage.

125
00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:47.772
For god sake can you
all not be after that mansion?

126
00:10:48.022 --> 00:10:49.274
I'm not after anything, okay?

127
00:10:49.524 --> 00:10:52.002
Pity you're not the landlord but
there's no need to get so cheesed off.

128
00:10:52.026 --> 00:10:55.381
I'm not getting cheesed off!

129
00:10:55.405 --> 00:10:58.509
Nor do I fancy being the landlord
of that godforsaken dilapidated mansion...

130
00:10:58.533 --> 00:11:01.053
One kick and there
won't be any of it left.

131
00:11:01.077 --> 00:11:04.348
Fine... kick it and stop blabbering... and
just don't get cheesed off...

132
00:11:04.372 --> 00:11:06.892
I am not cheesed off, ok?

133
00:11:06.916 --> 00:11:09.019
It's 4 pm already, sir...

134
00:11:09.043 --> 00:11:10.187
Wait, don't open yet...

135
00:11:10.211 --> 00:11:11.981
I'll see you next week...

136
00:11:12.005 --> 00:11:14.382
...with that chocolate biscuit...

137
00:11:14.799 --> 00:11:17.927
I'm not that poor that I can't buy
a damn chocolate biscuit for you.

138
00:11:19.762 --> 00:11:21.139
It's late...

139
00:11:29.647 --> 00:11:30.916
See you.

140
00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:31.940
Yeah.

141
00:11:43.703 --> 00:11:47.040
Bhaiyya,
this weighing scale is faulty.

142
00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:49.852
What do you expect me to do? Sit on it?

143
00:11:49.876 --> 00:11:51.228
How about paying up for last two months?

144
00:11:51.252 --> 00:11:52.879
Of course I will.

145
00:11:53.379 --> 00:11:55.673
Then do that first!!

146
00:12:15.902 --> 00:12:18.905
What you doing here like a snoopy
sewer rat, looking for breadcrumbs... huh?

147
00:12:19.656 --> 00:12:23.034
Are you increasing the
rent from this month or next?

148
00:12:23.576 --> 00:12:27.056
'Cause your trashy scoofer
existence is getting unbearable you see.

149
00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.874
Now what can I say
about your tolerance level.

150
00:12:30.291 --> 00:12:31.918
As for rent...

151
00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:36.130
...this is what it is, take it
or leave it and just so you know,

152
00:12:36.673 --> 00:12:40.176
we're never vacating this place.
Goodnight!

153
00:12:40.927 --> 00:12:46.367
Don't you dare come between
me and my mansion! Or else...

154
00:12:46.391 --> 00:12:49.143
With one leg already in grave,
are you threatening me?

155
00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:51.121
Look I'll just call
the university goons...

156
00:12:51.145 --> 00:12:53.898
...and all your dreams of mansion
will turn into a nightmare...

157
00:12:57.276 --> 00:12:58.903
So just chill.

158
00:13:21.175 --> 00:13:27.056
Oh I'll show you what a nightmare is!

159
00:13:39.819 --> 00:13:44.866
Neetu... go shower now!
Always wasting time.

160
00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:53.393
What?

161
00:13:53.417 --> 00:13:58.897
Parking slip, 50 rupees everyday.

162
00:13:58.921 --> 00:14:00.590
House tax has increased...

163
00:14:01.049 --> 00:14:04.427
Are you a twit? Or you think I am one?

164
00:14:04.677 --> 00:14:06.071
Now move...

165
00:14:06.095 --> 00:14:07.406
No, I won't let you.

166
00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.491
Gawd... tch... am getting late
for work... move...!

167
00:14:09.515 --> 00:14:13.394
Then just pay up and take your bike...

168
00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:16.165
But you haven't charged
a penny from Sayyad and Mishraji...

169
00:14:16.189 --> 00:14:18.983
Even they have their bicycles
and scooter parked here.

170
00:14:19.233 --> 00:14:23.422
Yeah but they're not the ones
who pay 30 bucks as house rent!

171
00:14:23.446 --> 00:14:26.258
Just back off,
Mirza, and play with those goats there...

172
00:14:26.282 --> 00:14:29.035
...you've no idea what I can do to you.

173
00:14:29.368 --> 00:14:34.016
Oh really?
The day I throw you outta here...

174
00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:39.462
...lock stock and barrel...
you'll land in hell Mister...

175
00:14:39.796 --> 00:14:45.051
Not even a dog will come and
piss on your face... we'll see then.

176
00:14:54.894 --> 00:14:57.998
Am not scared of anyone...

177
00:14:58.022 --> 00:15:01.710
This is my mansion...

178
00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:06.673
Not your damn parking... is that clear?

179
00:15:06.697 --> 00:15:08.383
Ya ya I got scared.

180
00:15:08.407 --> 00:15:09.968
This is my mansion...

181
00:15:09.992 --> 00:15:12.370
Dare you come again with your bike.

182
00:15:13.454 --> 00:15:16.040
You want to grab my house...
dare you even think...

183
00:15:16.666 --> 00:15:22.022
- C'mmon... show me... anyone...?
- Mirza, Baankey is gone!

184
00:15:22.046 --> 00:15:25.049
-I'll throw all of you outta here...

185
00:15:54.912 --> 00:15:57.516
Just the cleaning of this
chandelier would be 500 bucks...

186
00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.018
...and then the bulb etc...

187
00:16:00.042 --> 00:16:03.379
It's antique so nothing
less than 2000 rupees.

188
00:16:04.005 --> 00:16:06.299
It's all glasswork... one thousand.

189
00:16:07.258 --> 00:16:08.258
One thousand?

190
00:16:10.261 --> 00:16:14.056
- Or nothing...
- Tch... uh... wait...

191
00:16:16.726 --> 00:16:18.978
Okay one thousand it is...

192
00:16:22.899 --> 00:16:27.153
Go ahead quietly.

193
00:16:28.988 --> 00:16:30.448
Careful...

194
00:16:39.373 --> 00:16:41.417
I need a minute with her...

195
00:16:46.839 --> 00:16:49.926
She's up in flames...

196
00:16:51.677 --> 00:16:53.387
Let him in...

197
00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:06.943
Umm... Begum... my this month's
allowance is all spent...

198
00:17:07.443 --> 00:17:09.987
I was wondering if I could get...

199
00:17:10.404 --> 00:17:15.034
What about the rent from the tenants...

200
00:17:15.493 --> 00:17:17.119
Who's going to get that...?

201
00:17:17.495 --> 00:17:21.350
Oh leave that on me...
I'll get the rent out of those idiots...

202
00:17:21.374 --> 00:17:25.544
There's some lose currency in that box...

203
00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:27.546
...make do with that for now.

204
00:17:28.297 --> 00:17:29.025
Sure...

205
00:17:29.049 --> 00:17:34.154
And then for a few days
just stay out of my sight...

206
00:17:34.178 --> 00:17:35.596
Sure... sure...

207
00:17:45.481 --> 00:17:47.483
- How much...?
- 20 bucks...

208
00:17:48.276 --> 00:17:49.652
That's it?!

209
00:17:56.367 --> 00:17:57.785
Where is Mirza now?

210
00:17:58.035 --> 00:18:00.079
Hasn't come out of
Uncle Sayyad's room yet...

211
00:18:00.454 --> 00:18:02.039
Ok, keep at it...

212
00:18:05.459 --> 00:18:06.270
Ya, he's out.

213
00:18:06.294 --> 00:18:07.334
Where is he going next...?

214
00:18:07.503 --> 00:18:08.397
Coming here!

215
00:18:08.421 --> 00:18:09.421
Keep a watch.

216
00:18:10.006 --> 00:18:10.900
Oh he's almost here.

217
00:18:10.924 --> 00:18:11.924
Quick... get here...

218
00:18:14.927 --> 00:18:17.221
C'mmon... fast... give that cold strip...

219
00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.474
Lie down...

220
00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:26.731
Uh... am here... that's the rent receipt...

221
00:18:31.944 --> 00:18:35.031
What happened... fever?

222
00:18:35.448 --> 00:18:38.534
Since two days and I don't
even have money to buy medicines...

223
00:18:39.785 --> 00:18:41.096
...please don't ask for the rent today...

224
00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.663
This month too!

225
00:18:44.915 --> 00:18:46.435
Hey, it's not as if
your wheat mill has shut down...

226
00:18:46.459 --> 00:18:48.377
Ya, but the wheat produce got ruined.

227
00:18:49.462 --> 00:18:51.148
So no one's coming to get the flour...

228
00:18:51.172 --> 00:18:55.384
There's not a morsel at home, Baankey...

229
00:18:57.303 --> 00:19:00.806
We'll have to sell off this mixer...

230
00:19:01.557 --> 00:19:04.810
Yeah... how else to feed your sisters...

231
00:19:27.917 --> 00:19:29.168
That's a microwave.

232
00:19:30.294 --> 00:19:32.171
Food warmer...

233
00:19:33.214 --> 00:19:35.883
Yesterday the rice dish
got heated up in just 2 minutes...

234
00:19:40.805 --> 00:19:44.934
Evidently the crooks are partying...

235
00:19:46.227 --> 00:19:48.938
...well then I must provide the roast.

236
00:19:51.065 --> 00:19:52.385
Couldn't you keep your trap shut?

237
00:19:52.483 --> 00:19:54.902
Brainless...

238
00:20:03.369 --> 00:20:06.080
Now let's see how you eat
your rice dish... heated up!

239
00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:09.101
What's with this power cut?!

240
00:20:09.125 --> 00:20:11.520
Go check it out!

241
00:20:11.544 --> 00:20:14.088
Am sure it's Mirza again!

242
00:20:15.881 --> 00:20:19.444
Now aren't you gonna
leave that throne Mishra ji?

243
00:20:19.468 --> 00:20:21.279
Am not sitting on a throne...

244
00:20:21.303 --> 00:20:22.614
Third time since morning...

245
00:20:22.638 --> 00:20:23.638
Wait...

246
00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:30.813
And you carry those cheap
magazines inside Mishraji...?

247
00:20:32.523 --> 00:20:34.358
What happened?
Did you fall down?

248
00:20:36.026 --> 00:20:39.381
- No... Then?
- Uncle Mirza... he...

249
00:20:39.405 --> 00:20:40.632
What did he do?

250
00:20:40.656 --> 00:20:43.844
I was cutting mangoes for 'Daadi Bi'...

251
00:20:43.868 --> 00:20:47.580
...from that I ate a piece or two...
suddenly Mirza started screaming...

252
00:20:47.955 --> 00:20:51.333
...that brother has grabbed the
house and sister is grabbing mangoes.

253
00:20:51.709 --> 00:20:54.462
And he made me spit out
whatever I had in my mouth...

254
00:20:54.712 --> 00:20:55.921
Alright stop crying...

255
00:20:56.589 --> 00:20:57.756
...get back to home...

256
00:20:59.592 --> 00:21:01.135
Mirza needs to explain this...

257
00:21:04.138 --> 00:21:05.806
Mishraji are you coming out or...

258
00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:11.729
- What fell down?
- What happened?!

259
00:21:12.563 --> 00:21:14.207
What the hell did you do Baankey?

260
00:21:14.231 --> 00:21:15.232
...you'll kill me...

261
00:21:16.442 --> 00:21:17.419
What happened, brother?

262
00:21:17.443 --> 00:21:18.379
How did this fall...?

263
00:21:18.403 --> 00:21:19.380
Was that a bomb blast...?

264
00:21:19.404 --> 00:21:20.922
This wall fell down!

265
00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:22.132
How did this happen?

266
00:21:22.156 --> 00:21:23.967
What are you doing here... go away...

267
00:21:23.991 --> 00:21:25.427
Mishraji... where are you...?

268
00:21:25.451 --> 00:21:27.095
See what Baankey has done...

269
00:21:27.119 --> 00:21:29.639
I just kept my hand there and...
was an old wall anyway...

270
00:21:29.663 --> 00:21:30.663
What did you do, Baankey?

271
00:21:30.748 --> 00:21:32.350
He's been in there for an hour!!

272
00:21:32.374 --> 00:21:34.519
Just because you ride a bike,
you think you can hit the wall?

273
00:21:34.543 --> 00:21:35.480
I don't get the connection!

274
00:21:35.504 --> 00:21:37.272
My time slot is at 8 every morning...

275
00:21:37.296 --> 00:21:39.483
I was here but he's
been inside for an hour...

276
00:21:39.507 --> 00:21:40.650
That too his third time!

277
00:21:40.674 --> 00:21:41.943
On top it he carries newspapers!

278
00:21:41.967 --> 00:21:45.655
We've already fixed our slots so...

279
00:21:45.679 --> 00:21:47.115
Why should he get more than 15 minutes?

280
00:21:47.139 --> 00:21:48.784
Who'll repair this wall now?

281
00:21:48.808 --> 00:21:50.184
What happened, Sheikhu?

282
00:21:56.106 --> 00:21:57.106
Toilet...

283
00:22:01.654 --> 00:22:03.673
God knows what he
does for an hour inside!

284
00:22:03.697 --> 00:22:05.991
Uh oh... Mirza is coming here...

285
00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:16.436
Listen... wait... wait...
let me sort it out first.

286
00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:17.437
I'm going.

287
00:22:17.461 --> 00:22:18.730
No you can't.

288
00:22:18.754 --> 00:22:20.482
These are old
bricks... obviously it had to...

289
00:22:20.506 --> 00:22:22.442
No... no...
I am asking how did it collapse?

290
00:22:22.466 --> 00:22:24.677
I just touched it with my foot
and it came down...

291
00:22:25.052 --> 00:22:26.446
When you don't get things repaired!

292
00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:27.888
- Move aside!
- Wait!

293
00:22:28.138 --> 00:22:29.991
Huh... you think you'll do
the damage and I'll let you go?

294
00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:31.201
Now you'll get this wall done...

295
00:22:31.225 --> 00:22:34.579
Never! Your mansion,
your problem... now get off my way...

296
00:22:34.603 --> 00:22:38.065
I won't... either you increase
the rent or vacate the place...

297
00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.252
Sucking on my blood, like a leech.

298
00:22:40.276 --> 00:22:42.462
Don't scream or you'll get an attack...

299
00:22:42.486 --> 00:22:44.631
...and if you pass away before Begum...
imagine what'll happen to this mansion...

300
00:22:44.655 --> 00:22:47.008
You have 24 hours to repair this...

301
00:22:47.032 --> 00:22:52.389
Even if I have 24 years,
I won't do it... you're the landlord... so...

302
00:22:52.413 --> 00:22:56.667
Yeah I am the landlord...
one with the lineage... so!

303
00:22:57.251 --> 00:22:58.331
And I care a damn about it!

304
00:22:58.586 --> 00:23:01.314
That's not fair Mirza...
he just pays 30 bucks...

305
00:23:01.338 --> 00:23:02.566
...and we pay 70.

306
00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:03.733
Which latrine are we going to use now?

307
00:23:03.757 --> 00:23:06.987
We'll use theirs, the 70 rupee tenants!

308
00:23:07.011 --> 00:23:08.530
And Mirza has such a huge mansion...

309
00:23:08.554 --> 00:23:10.794
...am sure we can find many
hidden corners to defecate...

310
00:23:10.889 --> 00:23:11.974
Move...

311
00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:17.563
Oh! He left.

312
00:23:19.023 --> 00:23:20.316
Broke the wall...

313
00:23:26.572 --> 00:23:34.121
That's it... it's all locked now...
no one uses my toilets...

314
00:24:09.657 --> 00:24:12.093
Brother... brother...

315
00:24:12.117 --> 00:24:13.117
What is it...?

316
00:24:13.577 --> 00:24:14.870
I need to use the washroom...

317
00:24:15.579 --> 00:24:16.747
Get up...

318
00:24:17.206 --> 00:24:19.458
Go downstairs... am awake...

319
00:24:19.833 --> 00:24:22.594
Mirza has locked up every toilet...
and he's sleeping right outside...

320
00:24:23.045 --> 00:24:24.254
Please wake up!

321
00:24:29.802 --> 00:24:31.011
Where is he?

322
00:24:31.345 --> 00:24:32.596
Here...

323
00:24:35.015 --> 00:24:36.015
Let's see.

324
00:24:52.741 --> 00:24:56.286
Call Mishraji... quick...

325
00:25:48.213 --> 00:25:50.299
Mirza... how come you landed here...?

326
00:25:59.183 --> 00:26:00.702
Ya... stop.

327
00:26:00.726 --> 00:26:04.330
He picked up my bed and threw me
out of my house while I was sleeping...

328
00:26:04.354 --> 00:26:07.459
He's locked the toilets... my three sisters...
my mother... are they supposed to go out in the open?

329
00:26:07.483 --> 00:26:09.026
One second... relax...

330
00:26:13.113 --> 00:26:15.282
Sir... why did he throw me out...

331
00:26:15.657 --> 00:26:19.721
Listen to me... till the time
the toilet wall is not made,

332
00:26:19.745 --> 00:26:23.558
you'll have to provide
alternate toilets for the women...

333
00:26:23.582 --> 00:26:25.769
No, why should I? He broke the wall...

334
00:26:25.793 --> 00:26:30.023
My fancy toilets are not
for pedestrians like him...

335
00:26:30.047 --> 00:26:31.816
But he's your tenant... and...

336
00:26:31.840 --> 00:26:34.194
And whatever damages happen,
water electricity expenses...

337
00:26:34.218 --> 00:26:35.987
...they all have to be
borne by the landlord...

338
00:26:36.011 --> 00:26:37.489
...we've been paying the rent
for last 70 years...

339
00:26:37.513 --> 00:26:39.783
How did the wall collapse?

340
00:26:39.807 --> 00:26:41.743
How do I know...

341
00:26:41.767 --> 00:26:44.454
...I wasn't sitting inside
the brick that I would know...

342
00:26:44.478 --> 00:26:45.914
...how it broke.

343
00:26:45.938 --> 00:26:48.524
Just see what a doped out
uncivilized obnoxious guy he is!

344
00:26:48.982 --> 00:26:51.836
My 100 year old mansion...
won't let then grab it.

345
00:26:51.860 --> 00:26:54.380
Who's grabbing it...?

346
00:26:54.404 --> 00:26:56.532
And we're discussing the toilet...
not mansion...

347
00:26:56.949 --> 00:27:00.553
So keep your trap shut.

348
00:27:00.577 --> 00:27:01.995
Guys, can we focus on the wall?

349
00:27:02.246 --> 00:27:03.914
Who's going to repair it...?

350
00:27:04.164 --> 00:27:05.433
- Who are these people?
- Mirza or Baankey?

351
00:27:05.457 --> 00:27:09.437
Uh... tch... look Uncle,
these tenants have been staying for years...

352
00:27:09.461 --> 00:27:10.855
...so you can't just throw them out.

353
00:27:10.879 --> 00:27:12.714
You can't throw us out!

354
00:27:13.006 --> 00:27:15.425
Stop being a buffoon...
Because you're a tenant,

355
00:27:16.009 --> 00:27:19.364
you'll never become a landlord even if you've
been staying for 100 years in the same house.

356
00:27:19.388 --> 00:27:21.348
Never ever!

357
00:27:21.682 --> 00:27:24.661
And for any further information,
go to the civil courts...

358
00:27:24.685 --> 00:27:27.396
...this matter belongs there,
not with the police...

359
00:27:27.980 --> 00:27:29.231
Get out now...

360
00:27:42.369 --> 00:27:44.371
That I'm useless...

361
00:27:44.663 --> 00:27:47.291
I repeat... that I'm useless.

362
00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:50.103
I've proven it long back.

363
00:27:50.127 --> 00:27:52.504
I haven't come across a
bigger scoundrel than Baankey...

364
00:27:53.589 --> 00:27:55.191
...he's eyeing your mansion.

365
00:27:55.215 --> 00:27:58.135
And the police maintains the matter
belongs to the civil court...

366
00:27:58.802 --> 00:28:01.680
...and that old woman...
that witch from the dungeons...

367
00:28:02.431 --> 00:28:04.308
...she's also refusing to die...

368
00:28:04.558 --> 00:28:12.107
Have faith in God Mirza...
Begum will die this winter...

369
00:28:14.151 --> 00:28:16.004
Are you sure she'll die...?

370
00:28:16.028 --> 00:28:17.404
Of course!

371
00:28:17.654 --> 00:28:21.241
See what I am saying
is these tenants of yours...

372
00:28:21.575 --> 00:28:24.912
...should pay at least 500 bucks each.

373
00:28:25.579 --> 00:28:27.581
I mean that is the going market rate...

374
00:28:29.416 --> 00:28:33.587
I'll look for a lawyer...
but you stay with that thought...

375
00:28:42.804 --> 00:28:47.476
How much is 2,500 multiplied by 12?

376
00:28:47.726 --> 00:28:51.414
Ummm... 5 by 12 is 60... and...

377
00:28:51.438 --> 00:28:53.374
- 30,000
- What?

378
00:28:53.398 --> 00:28:54.398
30,000

379
00:28:55.067 --> 00:28:58.362
- 30,000? Really?!
- How much is this? - 90 rupees.

380
00:28:59.029 --> 00:29:02.282
- Are you alright?
- Yeah... I'm fine... I'm fine...

381
00:29:02.866 --> 00:29:04.469
- Get him up.
- I'm fine.

382
00:29:04.493 --> 00:29:06.721
30,000?!

383
00:29:06.745 --> 00:29:08.806
Yes... yes... are you okay?

384
00:29:08.830 --> 00:29:10.016
Give me your hand.

385
00:29:10.040 --> 00:29:11.458
Sit, relax.

386
00:29:14.586 --> 00:29:18.548
Sit here... Relax.

387
00:29:22.970 --> 00:29:24.554
30,000?!

388
00:29:44.491 --> 00:29:49.246
Hey... excuse me... what are you doing?

389
00:29:50.914 --> 00:29:54.167
Am talking to you... here, this side.

390
00:29:56.169 --> 00:29:58.130
Can't you see am making a pudding...

391
00:29:59.548 --> 00:30:01.651
How can you take pictures
without permission? Stop it.

392
00:30:01.675 --> 00:30:04.678
Do you take permission
to click historical monuments?

393
00:30:06.221 --> 00:30:09.575
And I don't even see any board
here that prohibits photography...

394
00:30:09.599 --> 00:30:11.786
Don't act smart... I stay here...

395
00:30:11.810 --> 00:30:14.438
...one whack from me,
you'll be on the ground on all fours...

396
00:30:14.730 --> 00:30:17.024
Look Mister,
to begin with, mind your language,

397
00:30:18.775 --> 00:30:20.586
because as per the orders
of the Supreme court,

398
00:30:20.610 --> 00:30:23.030
no matter how long you
may've grabbed the house for...

399
00:30:24.489 --> 00:30:27.034
...you don't have any rights
on the house...

400
00:30:27.868 --> 00:30:31.455
Once a tenant always a tenant.

401
00:30:33.290 --> 00:30:35.792
And who the hell are you?

402
00:30:36.334 --> 00:30:39.880
Lawyer? Police? Army?

403
00:30:40.422 --> 00:30:42.049
I am archeology!

404
00:30:47.345 --> 00:30:52.017
In charge of the ruins... and that you're
a duffer, it's evident from your face.

405
00:30:52.934 --> 00:30:55.479
Am not such a duffer that
you'd fool me with a candy.

406
00:30:56.396 --> 00:30:59.191
Supreme court is in Delhi
and this is Lucknow...

407
00:30:59.733 --> 00:31:07.699
Here, might is right... so get outta here...
right away... jump off that damn tree...

408
00:31:09.576 --> 00:31:12.370
Why are you still sitting
there like a monkey?

409
00:31:13.580 --> 00:31:15.165
I won't be able to jump.

410
00:31:15.916 --> 00:31:17.793
Come down just as you climbed up.

411
00:31:19.669 --> 00:31:21.588
I need help... you see... I've arthritis.

412
00:31:21.922 --> 00:31:22.922
Here...

413
00:31:32.432 --> 00:31:34.392
Doctor says...

414
00:31:36.353 --> 00:31:40.816
...getting down is more difficult
for the knees than climbing up...

415
00:31:43.443 --> 00:31:46.083
And... a... that toilet wall...
you haven't got it repaired, right?

416
00:31:46.238 --> 00:31:49.092
No... why?

417
00:31:49.116 --> 00:31:50.867
Just do as I say...

418
00:31:51.493 --> 00:31:54.013
I am Gyanesh Shukla...
and right now I am in a bit of a hurry...

419
00:31:54.412 --> 00:31:55.848
I'll speak to you later.

420
00:31:55.872 --> 00:31:57.582
Rickshaw!

421
00:31:59.668 --> 00:32:00.668
But you stay in touch.

422
00:32:01.545 --> 00:32:04.273
Come on, hurry up!

423
00:32:04.297 --> 00:32:05.465
Aliganj.

424
00:32:09.678 --> 00:32:11.054
Bye.

425
00:32:18.228 --> 00:32:23.024
For example Mohenjo-daro and Harappa...

426
00:32:23.441 --> 00:32:25.722
So these places were dug up
and whatever stuff came out...

427
00:32:25.944 --> 00:32:28.446
...whatever glass bowls...spoon etc.

428
00:32:28.697 --> 00:32:31.992
The archaeology guys take it away
and display it in museums.

429
00:32:33.034 --> 00:32:35.412
Sometimes, if need be,
they take away the place itself.

430
00:32:35.745 --> 00:32:37.038
And convert it into a museum.

431
00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:41.686
What happened brother...
why are you staring blank?

432
00:32:41.710 --> 00:32:43.503
Looks like brother didn't get it...

433
00:32:44.588 --> 00:32:46.423
There is nothing to not understand...

434
00:32:46.923 --> 00:32:48.693
All I am thinking is we don't have
any such bowls or spoons...

435
00:32:48.717 --> 00:32:50.517
...nor is Mohenjo-daro
in Lucknow district...

436
00:32:51.219 --> 00:32:52.219
Just wondering.

437
00:32:53.388 --> 00:32:54.388
Whats' there to be blank!

438
00:32:55.932 --> 00:32:59.394
Why don't you take your grade 12 exam...

439
00:32:59.936 --> 00:33:01.336
Don't worry we'll help you study...

440
00:33:01.479 --> 00:33:03.356
Well, this is in grade 10 syllabus.

441
00:33:04.524 --> 00:33:06.284
Ya so we'll help you
with grade 10 as well...

442
00:33:30.717 --> 00:33:33.720
That's it... stop here...

443
00:33:34.846 --> 00:33:36.723
Please wait here till I come back.

444
00:33:48.735 --> 00:33:49.735
Are you Mirza?

445
00:33:50.320 --> 00:33:51.320
Uh hmm...

446
00:33:53.990 --> 00:33:57.637
I'm official... archaeology... move.

447
00:33:57.661 --> 00:33:59.829
- Excuse me...
- Where are you going inside...?

448
00:34:01.915 --> 00:34:04.334
I am Gyanesh Shukla.

449
00:34:05.126 --> 00:34:06.562
Baankey knows me.

450
00:34:06.586 --> 00:34:07.671
What are you doing?

451
00:34:09.673 --> 00:34:11.400
You haven't got that
wall repaired, right?

452
00:34:11.424 --> 00:34:12.424
Which one?

453
00:34:12.676 --> 00:34:14.135
The toilet wall you idiot...

454
00:34:16.805 --> 00:34:22.060
- Who the hell are you... get me some tea...
- Go, you go...

455
00:34:28.984 --> 00:34:32.195
- Photo?
- Because I am archaeology.

456
00:34:32.570 --> 00:34:33.340
What?

457
00:34:33.364 --> 00:34:34.572
For the records.

458
00:34:35.323 --> 00:34:36.408
Why are you going there...?

459
00:34:39.160 --> 00:34:41.913
You can't go there...
It's the women's section.

460
00:34:46.960 --> 00:34:48.295
Your mother is still alive?

461
00:34:49.004 --> 00:34:51.131
- Who is that?
- No idea.

462
00:34:51.506 --> 00:34:53.133
Come please...

463
00:35:53.485 --> 00:35:56.571
Look today is a Sunday and I like
to do all the official conversations...

464
00:35:58.490 --> 00:36:00.210
...on working day,
so see you another day...

465
00:36:01.368 --> 00:36:03.578
How the hell did this mansion slip out...

466
00:36:04.120 --> 00:36:04.579
Huh?

467
00:36:04.871 --> 00:36:06.790
Nothing... doesn't matter.

468
00:36:08.500 --> 00:36:10.126
Just wait for an
official letter now...

469
00:36:11.044 --> 00:36:12.670
The fun is about to begin.

470
00:36:13.004 --> 00:36:14.004
Huh?

471
00:36:15.048 --> 00:36:16.132
Let's go.

472
00:36:31.272 --> 00:36:32.291
Let's go.

473
00:36:32.315 --> 00:36:34.877
Who sent him to my mansion...?

474
00:36:34.901 --> 00:36:39.155
How dare he get here... has
to be one of these idiots.

475
00:36:42.534 --> 00:36:48.206
- Send these to Guptaji
- So you called Gyanesh, didn't you?

476
00:36:50.375 --> 00:36:51.186
What? Did he come again?

477
00:36:51.210 --> 00:36:53.002
That means you only called him...

478
00:36:54.045 --> 00:36:56.565
Are you out of your mind...
Why would I call him...

479
00:36:56.589 --> 00:36:58.275
I'm certain it has to be you.

480
00:36:58.299 --> 00:37:00.694
How else did he come to know
about the toilet wall...?

481
00:37:00.718 --> 00:37:03.280
I'm not the only one
who stays in that house...

482
00:37:03.304 --> 00:37:04.407
Anybody could have called him.

483
00:37:04.431 --> 00:37:06.659
Oh you are such a fox!

484
00:37:06.683 --> 00:37:09.995
Oh well... then you are
a broken bone of an anaconda...

485
00:37:10.019 --> 00:37:12.873
Go... wipe your filthy
face, you rotten mongoose...

486
00:37:12.897 --> 00:37:14.732
- Oh you want to?
- Yes!

487
00:37:15.108 --> 00:37:19.279
C'mmon... try me... you lousy lowly man.

488
00:37:22.782 --> 00:37:23.718
Keep that back.

489
00:37:23.742 --> 00:37:25.219
Don't you dare come close.

490
00:37:25.243 --> 00:37:28.288
Huh! I'll do what I feel like.

491
00:37:28.580 --> 00:37:30.457
Weirdo!

492
00:37:37.881 --> 00:37:38.881
I'll see you tomorrow.

493
00:37:43.887 --> 00:37:44.887
What happened?

494
00:37:44.971 --> 00:37:45.680
It's okay... come.

495
00:37:45.972 --> 00:37:47.098
Is everything okay?

496
00:37:47.807 --> 00:37:48.807
Have you lost it?

497
00:37:49.142 --> 00:37:51.954
Or do you suffer from night blindness
that you cannot see what's going on?

498
00:37:51.978 --> 00:37:53.018
Mirza has sent you, right?

499
00:37:54.772 --> 00:37:56.649
Ya he's the third guy, so?!

500
00:37:57.025 --> 00:37:59.861
What's your problem...?
I didn't enjoy with the others...

501
00:38:01.029 --> 00:38:02.238
Am I really the third one?

502
00:38:03.573 --> 00:38:05.867
Looks like your male ego
has been squashed like a lemon.

503
00:38:06.659 --> 00:38:07.979
In that case you can leave now...

504
00:38:08.578 --> 00:38:10.264
- Obviously I'm not going to hang around here.
- Yeah get lost.

505
00:38:10.288 --> 00:38:11.581
Strange woman?!

506
00:38:16.544 --> 00:38:17.544
Get lost!

507
00:38:19.047 --> 00:38:21.883
Keep your hands off me!
What?!

508
00:38:25.720 --> 00:38:28.264
Government official? He came again?!

509
00:38:28.598 --> 00:38:29.933
That archaeology fellow?

510
00:38:30.725 --> 00:38:31.911
I smell trouble.

511
00:38:31.935 --> 00:38:35.396
Look if any government guy comes,
you'll tell me first... is that clear?

512
00:38:36.940 --> 00:38:38.650
You'll get your 50 bucks...

513
00:38:43.154 --> 00:38:45.448
What are you staring at?
Don't you have to get to school?

514
00:38:45.698 --> 00:38:46.282
Yes...

515
00:38:46.699 --> 00:38:49.202
Why've you worn my top?

516
00:38:49.953 --> 00:38:51.514
I couldn't find my top.

517
00:38:51.538 --> 00:38:57.126
Wait... wait...
get off the rickshaw... get off.

518
00:38:59.295 --> 00:39:00.481
Don't do that Mirza.

519
00:39:00.505 --> 00:39:02.257
Oh you mind your own business.

520
00:39:04.551 --> 00:39:08.888
They've no penny for rent but
they've all the money for luxuries... huh.

521
00:39:15.895 --> 00:39:17.063
Come.

522
00:39:35.623 --> 00:39:39.460
Are you Christopher?

523
00:39:40.795 --> 00:39:42.463
Eh... Pandey Ji...

524
00:39:42.880 --> 00:39:45.109
Christopher Clarke.

525
00:39:45.133 --> 00:39:50.930
I specialize in getting house vacated
...and also in getting it nabbed.

526
00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:53.617
I mean how do I trust you...?

527
00:39:53.641 --> 00:39:54.684
Trust?

528
00:39:55.643 --> 00:39:59.081
Look sir, I speak
in English at home.

529
00:39:59.105 --> 00:40:01.065
I eat lunch and dinner for food.

530
00:40:01.399 --> 00:40:04.753
If you have ever heard of that
famous builder in the city, Mun Mun ji.

531
00:40:04.777 --> 00:40:06.904
Well I am very close to him.

532
00:40:07.488 --> 00:40:10.617
And I am not sitting here in this library
to read some useless novel.

533
00:40:11.075 --> 00:40:13.995
I'm here to make points because
I have to get a house nabbed.

534
00:40:14.662 --> 00:40:15.662
Understood?

535
00:40:15.872 --> 00:40:17.415
Mishra... look after this please.

536
00:40:18.291 --> 00:40:19.709
I'll see you later.

537
00:40:20.418 --> 00:40:21.419
Let's go.

538
00:40:22.462 --> 00:40:24.172
And you don't have
to get the house nabbed.

539
00:40:24.839 --> 00:40:27.467
You've to get your house vacated, right?

540
00:40:34.307 --> 00:40:36.619
It's not some property...
It's my mansion.

541
00:40:36.643 --> 00:40:39.496
I know I know it's a mansion.
Here.

542
00:40:39.520 --> 00:40:42.207
- But in legal language it's called property.
- Ok.

543
00:40:42.231 --> 00:40:44.543
And there is not just one
but many property laws.

544
00:40:44.567 --> 00:40:46.170
We will write a plea
and submit it in the court.

545
00:40:46.194 --> 00:40:48.255
We'll give evidence.
Sit please.

546
00:40:48.279 --> 00:40:50.359
They'll get the notice
and the house will be vacated.

547
00:40:51.741 --> 00:40:53.427
Is it that simple?

548
00:40:53.451 --> 00:40:55.495
Of course...
I just need property papers.

549
00:40:55.745 --> 00:40:56.745
Huh?

550
00:40:57.455 --> 00:40:58.807
Papers?

551
00:40:58.831 --> 00:41:01.310
Yeah. Documentation.

552
00:41:01.334 --> 00:41:03.187
All the records that have been...

553
00:41:03.211 --> 00:41:05.171
...maintained between
the landlord and the tenant.

554
00:41:05.630 --> 00:41:07.107
Those papers...
Pandeyji mentioned that...

555
00:41:07.131 --> 00:41:11.111
...the property is in the name
of your wife and now she is no more.

556
00:41:11.135 --> 00:41:13.012
No no she hasn't died.

557
00:41:13.429 --> 00:41:15.056
That's what I'm waiting for.

558
00:41:15.515 --> 00:41:17.100
Look the mansion is mine.

559
00:41:17.392 --> 00:41:19.477
It's just that it's not on my name yet.

560
00:41:19.811 --> 00:41:21.121
Oh... ok... ok.

561
00:41:21.145 --> 00:41:22.665
There is yet another problem.

562
00:41:22.689 --> 00:41:24.083
What?

563
00:41:24.107 --> 00:41:29.487
That archaeology fellow has
also started intruding in between.

564
00:41:29.904 --> 00:41:32.174
Why would an archaeology guy be interested
in a 3 or 4 bedroom property...?

565
00:41:32.198 --> 00:41:33.467
I don't get it.

566
00:41:33.491 --> 00:41:36.119
I have been telling you
that it is a mansion.

567
00:41:36.661 --> 00:41:39.372
- Not some tiny house.
- You mean a real mansion?

568
00:41:39.664 --> 00:41:46.129
Yes, which Begum got from
her father and he got from his father.

569
00:41:47.088 --> 00:41:49.483
Oh... now I get it.

570
00:41:49.507 --> 00:41:52.027
What was that 'oh' for?

571
00:41:52.051 --> 00:41:54.178
You see the day Begum dies.

572
00:41:55.388 --> 00:42:01.144
There'll be at least 50 more greedy guys
knocking on your doorstep... overnight.

573
00:42:01.394 --> 00:42:02.394
Are you getting me?

574
00:42:07.650 --> 00:42:10.027
That is exactly why
I did not have any child.

575
00:42:10.653 --> 00:42:13.090
So that this mansion remains only mine.

576
00:42:13.114 --> 00:42:18.161
For such properties,
even kids get born overnight.

577
00:42:19.120 --> 00:42:23.124
Such mansions don't have
single clear ownership ever.

578
00:42:23.750 --> 00:42:27.712
So you need to find out who is dead,
who is alive.

579
00:42:28.921 --> 00:42:30.521
Can't sit around any more, 'Sherlock...'

580
00:42:31.257 --> 00:42:32.341
Sherlock?

581
00:42:32.717 --> 00:42:33.926
Yes, Sherlock!

582
00:42:38.639 --> 00:42:41.642
Who's dead... who's alive.

583
00:42:42.810 --> 00:42:44.228
Where do I get this?

584
00:42:45.188 --> 00:42:48.232
I'll have to ask Begum.

585
00:42:48.900 --> 00:42:50.485
Who's dead... who's alive.

586
00:42:57.158 --> 00:43:00.036
This one is my eldest sister.

587
00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:03.724
The one with the dripping nose.

588
00:43:03.748 --> 00:43:07.794
She should be dead by now?

589
00:43:08.211 --> 00:43:10.856
I mean who all are alive...?

590
00:43:10.880 --> 00:43:14.258
I don't really remember...
few of them are alive... few, dead.

591
00:43:14.717 --> 00:43:17.929
This one looks quite old.

592
00:43:18.221 --> 00:43:21.325
By that logic, you too are old
and should be dead by now.

593
00:43:21.349 --> 00:43:25.186
Why are you alive?!

594
00:43:26.562 --> 00:43:28.832
So who all are still around?

595
00:43:28.856 --> 00:43:31.043
I told you I don't remember.

596
00:43:31.067 --> 00:43:33.670
Ae Dulhain, where is my betel leaf?

597
00:43:33.694 --> 00:43:35.130
Don't worry, I'll help you.

598
00:43:35.154 --> 00:43:40.368
See this is the family photograph taken
during your grandfather's second wedding.

599
00:43:40.618 --> 00:43:41.970
Is it?

600
00:43:41.994 --> 00:43:47.726
Look at this one...
your elder grandma had 11 kids...

601
00:43:47.750 --> 00:43:49.710
...and your younger grandma had 9.

602
00:43:50.044 --> 00:43:54.525
Your father was your
younger grandma's 6th born.

603
00:43:54.549 --> 00:43:55.967
Is it?

604
00:43:56.217 --> 00:43:59.071
- Mirza...? come close.
- Uh... yeah.

605
00:43:59.095 --> 00:44:01.097
Come closer.

606
00:44:01.556 --> 00:44:06.060
Did you and I get married
or did I elope with you?

607
00:44:06.602 --> 00:44:08.437
What are you saying, Begum!

608
00:44:09.522 --> 00:44:11.691
Of course we got married.

609
00:44:12.525 --> 00:44:15.027
I even paid you the traditional dues.

610
00:44:15.611 --> 00:44:18.090
So who did I elope with?

611
00:44:18.114 --> 00:44:20.533
That mongrel, Abdul Rehman.

612
00:44:20.992 --> 00:44:22.118
Anyway.

613
00:44:22.702 --> 00:44:28.183
Just tell me who all
are alive in your family.

614
00:44:28.207 --> 00:44:32.020
You seem to be after my family.

615
00:44:32.044 --> 00:44:35.284
No... no... all I'm asking is... just the
way your eldest sister is still alive...

616
00:44:36.883 --> 00:44:38.676
...but your middle brother is dead...

617
00:44:39.051 --> 00:44:45.349
...so what about your other brothers
and sisters...are they around or...?

618
00:44:46.142 --> 00:44:49.228
Look I have not invited
anyone for the party.

619
00:44:49.645 --> 00:44:50.645
Is it clear?

620
00:44:51.147 --> 00:44:55.359
When Nehruji comes,
I'm going to complain about you...

621
00:44:55.735 --> 00:44:58.112
...and make sure that
he puts you behind the bars.

622
00:44:58.404 --> 00:45:00.031
These are all your family members only.

623
00:45:00.865 --> 00:45:02.950
Your brothers. Your sisters.

624
00:45:03.284 --> 00:45:10.458
Just think maybe there was a good news
that someone had passed away.

625
00:45:11.042 --> 00:45:14.354
- I mean...
- What do you mean? Just get lost.

626
00:45:14.378 --> 00:45:15.463
Fine... relax.

627
00:45:16.047 --> 00:45:19.091
- Hey you... get me something to eat.
- Sure.

628
00:45:19.717 --> 00:45:23.113
- Older sister is still alive...
- Old man is hanging

629
00:45:23.137 --> 00:45:26.349
- ...younger brother is dead.
- To threads of a torn long coat

630
00:45:29.352 --> 00:45:34.732
He is nearing death but he is not bothered
to change his mischievous ways

631
00:45:37.026 --> 00:45:45.026
He is disliked by everyone,
but he is happy doing mischief

632
00:45:47.870 --> 00:45:53.584
Huh! You wanted to nab my mansion...
there... now you come.

633
00:45:53.876 --> 00:45:57.046
- Oh! this got left out.
- He wanders aimlessly around

634
00:45:57.546 --> 00:46:00.776
- Let me see who enters.
- Every nook and corner

635
00:46:00.800 --> 00:46:04.387
Old man is hanging to threads
of a torn long coat

636
00:46:04.762 --> 00:46:07.115
Hey kids... get out... out!

637
00:46:07.139 --> 00:46:12.645
He is nearing death but he is not bothered
to change his mischievous ways

638
00:46:15.398 --> 00:46:16.732
What?

639
00:46:18.651 --> 00:46:19.771
When did he put these locks?

640
00:46:23.155 --> 00:46:24.740
There are more?!

641
00:46:37.378 --> 00:46:39.046
What is going on...?

642
00:46:52.476 --> 00:46:54.562
Saturn is of low...

643
00:46:55.062 --> 00:46:57.732
...but do you see the mount of Venus?

644
00:46:58.065 --> 00:47:00.109
- Everything is in these hands.
- Oh?

645
00:47:01.235 --> 00:47:03.422
- Now you see...
- Shukla ji.

646
00:47:03.446 --> 00:47:05.114
- Ya?
- It's me.

647
00:47:05.364 --> 00:47:06.782
Sit.

648
00:47:07.450 --> 00:47:09.869
I'll read your right palm
in the canteen... okay?

649
00:47:12.788 --> 00:47:13.873
Yes?

650
00:47:15.124 --> 00:47:17.084
You had come to my house...
without informing.

651
00:47:17.668 --> 00:47:20.772
- I've no idea what you're talking about
- You'd had climbed the tree... my place.

652
00:47:20.796 --> 00:47:22.796
And then you said to stay
in touch... Fatima Mahal.

653
00:47:23.049 --> 00:47:27.595
Right... Now I remember... so...
What brings you here?

654
00:47:29.680 --> 00:47:31.199
Bring me the files.

655
00:47:31.223 --> 00:47:35.495
Sir... Remember I had mentioned to you about...
Fatima Mahal.

656
00:47:35.519 --> 00:47:37.289
- Yeah?
- He's one of the tenants.

657
00:47:37.313 --> 00:47:42.169
Rentals have gone miserably up
in Lucknow... better start looking out.

658
00:47:42.193 --> 00:47:43.652
You let him know.

659
00:47:47.031 --> 00:47:48.271
What is going on Shukla ji ...?

660
00:47:48.365 --> 00:47:49.525
What are you intending to do?

661
00:47:50.034 --> 00:47:51.869
Why is he asking me
to look for a new house?

662
00:47:52.161 --> 00:47:53.996
And what have you spoken to Mirza ...?

663
00:47:54.830 --> 00:47:56.123
Let's step out for a bit.

664
00:47:57.208 --> 00:47:58.685
So she is not his mother?

665
00:47:58.709 --> 00:48:02.046
No... his wife... 17 years older than him.

666
00:48:03.631 --> 00:48:04.631
Ohh!

667
00:48:06.467 --> 00:48:09.027
That toilet wall... I hope
you haven't got it repaired, right...?

668
00:48:09.053 --> 00:48:10.322
Why are you after that wall?

669
00:48:10.346 --> 00:48:12.199
You have any idea how difficult
it is getting for us to manage.

670
00:48:12.223 --> 00:48:13.349
Shut up!

671
00:48:14.058 --> 00:48:16.058
Do not raise your voice,
it is a government office.

672
00:48:16.185 --> 00:48:18.466
Not Nixon market that you
yell and sell bargained clothes.

673
00:48:21.107 --> 00:48:25.528
I speak only in favour of your case.

674
00:48:27.196 --> 00:48:28.196
C'mmon.

675
00:48:31.242 --> 00:48:32.660
Hit here...
on the wall.

676
00:48:33.244 --> 00:48:34.328
Why?

677
00:48:34.912 --> 00:48:36.312
Pcch... you ask too many questions.

678
00:48:36.831 --> 00:48:38.040
Just do as I say.

679
00:48:42.044 --> 00:48:43.044
Harder!

680
00:48:46.757 --> 00:48:49.552
Did it collapse? No.

681
00:48:50.177 --> 00:48:52.096
Because this is how
the house walls need to be.

682
00:48:53.097 --> 00:48:55.766
Not like yours that one kick
and the entire building comes down.

683
00:48:59.395 --> 00:49:02.523
Maybe we all tenants can
collect some money and repair it.

684
00:49:03.232 --> 00:49:05.025
What about rest of the mansion?

685
00:49:05.734 --> 00:49:07.934
Today it is just one wall...
tomorrow it'll be the roof.

686
00:49:07.987 --> 00:49:09.029
Day after, the stairs.

687
00:49:09.780 --> 00:49:11.073
Do you guys have the money?

688
00:49:15.870 --> 00:49:18.998
But there are many people living
in such dilapidated buildings...

689
00:49:19.331 --> 00:49:22.144
...your government doesn't go around
taking the responsibility of helping them.

690
00:49:22.168 --> 00:49:25.379
Of course we don't... But we are taking
the responsibility of this mansion.

691
00:49:26.046 --> 00:49:29.006
Because if this comes crashing down,
trust me you won't find a single body.

692
00:49:33.804 --> 00:49:35.124
Let's go and grab some breakfast.

693
00:49:35.347 --> 00:49:36.473
I'm quite full.

694
00:49:36.724 --> 00:49:38.767
I am talking for myself.

695
00:49:39.643 --> 00:49:40.978
Come on.

696
00:49:43.856 --> 00:49:45.399
Musa Bagh...

697
00:49:45.816 --> 00:49:47.026
Dilkusha palace...

698
00:49:47.359 --> 00:49:48.444
Farhat Bakhsh palace...

699
00:49:48.777 --> 00:49:50.362
Imam Bara Chota Bara...

700
00:49:50.988 --> 00:49:52.698
Amin-ud-daula's Residency...

701
00:49:53.157 --> 00:49:55.093
Asif-ud-daula's Residency...

702
00:49:55.117 --> 00:49:57.119
Qaiser Bagh, Baradari...

703
00:49:57.661 --> 00:50:00.039
Now if you notice these are all...

704
00:50:00.998 --> 00:50:03.417
...historically important buildings.
Heritage.

705
00:50:04.835 --> 00:50:05.835
Now look here.

706
00:50:06.712 --> 00:50:08.106
Are you saying even trees
come under your authority?

707
00:50:08.130 --> 00:50:10.650
Trees, plants, rivers, canals,
roads, buildings... everything.

708
00:50:10.674 --> 00:50:11.967
Do you see this railing?

709
00:50:16.972 --> 00:50:18.572
Are you restoring this building as well?

710
00:50:18.891 --> 00:50:20.744
Oh no... not this useless building.

711
00:50:20.768 --> 00:50:22.228
We were passing by, so just stopped.

712
00:50:22.603 --> 00:50:24.730
How do you know all this, Shukla ji?

713
00:50:27.816 --> 00:50:30.569
I am the government and
the government knows everything.

714
00:50:49.838 --> 00:50:51.149
You know what my father says?

715
00:50:51.173 --> 00:50:52.173
What?

716
00:50:53.008 --> 00:50:55.153
That a man isn't rich
or poor because of his money.

717
00:50:55.177 --> 00:50:56.457
But because of his intelligence.

718
00:50:56.762 --> 00:50:58.347
And I'm beginning to feel that...

719
00:50:59.056 --> 00:51:00.242
...you are not only poor
because of your money.

720
00:51:00.266 --> 00:51:01.618
...but even because of a
total lack of intelligence.

721
00:51:01.642 --> 00:51:03.310
As if you are very intelligent!

722
00:51:03.894 --> 00:51:05.288
I'm not but at least I pretend to be.

723
00:51:05.312 --> 00:51:07.432
And by pretending over a
period of time I will become.

724
00:51:08.732 --> 00:51:10.001
What have I done now?

725
00:51:10.025 --> 00:51:13.195
That man kept rattling off such
big names of the British and Nawabs...

726
00:51:13.612 --> 00:51:15.548
...and you are such a nincompoop
that you stood quiet.

727
00:51:15.572 --> 00:51:18.009
If I was there I would
have pinned him down.

728
00:51:18.033 --> 00:51:21.554
And would have told him that I stay in
Fatima Mahal and not Taj Mahal.

729
00:51:21.578 --> 00:51:22.621
So just stay away.

730
00:51:24.456 --> 00:51:26.834
I was about to talk to mom about us.

731
00:51:27.293 --> 00:51:28.353
I don't think I'm going to do that now.

732
00:51:28.377 --> 00:51:30.658
Just because I called you nincompoop,
you got cheesed off.

733
00:51:31.213 --> 00:51:35.050
Fine... they've selected a guy for me.
Should I say yes?

734
00:51:35.676 --> 00:51:38.071
Don't bother calling
me for your wedding.

735
00:51:38.095 --> 00:51:41.598
I'm not an idiot to waste my
father's hundred bucks per plate on you.

736
00:51:43.809 --> 00:51:48.022
Stop clinging to me.
I'll drop you at the bus stop.

737
00:51:48.355 --> 00:51:50.795
I'm not taking the bus nor am
I interested in clinging to you.

738
00:51:51.025 --> 00:51:53.425
You picked me up from home,
so you better drop me back there.

739
00:52:14.006 --> 00:52:16.467
New ones are for Rs.100 and
second hand ones are for Rs.25/-

740
00:52:16.717 --> 00:52:18.028
Okay, give me Rs.20.

741
00:52:18.052 --> 00:52:19.136
- Rs.20?
- Rs.20.

742
00:52:19.803 --> 00:52:22.848
Just try and see if it fits.

743
00:52:23.474 --> 00:52:24.975
Oh my god!

744
00:52:29.521 --> 00:52:31.023
Aah! They're fine.

745
00:52:31.523 --> 00:52:32.775
I'll keep my old ones.

746
00:52:33.108 --> 00:52:34.777
Give me that other one.

747
00:52:37.988 --> 00:52:39.698
Where did you learn all this?

748
00:52:40.032 --> 00:52:44.036
I know all the hairstyles. See?

749
00:52:46.080 --> 00:52:47.080
Show.

750
00:52:48.040 --> 00:52:49.184
Ooh nice.

751
00:52:49.208 --> 00:52:51.794
Where will you go looking this stunning?

752
00:52:52.753 --> 00:52:54.463
Why should I tell?

753
00:52:54.838 --> 00:52:57.216
But I'm certainly
not taking Mirza with me.

754
00:52:57.466 --> 00:53:01.387
Oh that poor man will cry
so much... he'll die without you.

755
00:53:01.762 --> 00:53:04.032
He'll do none of that.

756
00:53:04.056 --> 00:53:06.725
Here... live all the tenants of Mirza.

757
00:53:07.309 --> 00:53:09.728
This whole lane.

758
00:53:11.105 --> 00:53:15.168
Begum's section is upstairs
and Mirza's downstairs.

759
00:53:15.192 --> 00:53:17.736
Oh she's sitting downstairs today.

760
00:53:18.612 --> 00:53:22.217
Greetings, Begum... how are you?

761
00:53:22.241 --> 00:53:24.034
Greetings.

762
00:53:24.326 --> 00:53:25.512
Do you recognise me?

763
00:53:25.536 --> 00:53:27.538
Uh... mm... yeah.

764
00:53:28.414 --> 00:53:30.416
If you've recognised me tell me my name.

765
00:53:31.834 --> 00:53:34.545
You're...

766
00:53:36.630 --> 00:53:38.382
Galileo!

767
00:53:39.675 --> 00:53:41.385
Hey Pandey ji,
come over here, will you?

768
00:53:41.718 --> 00:53:43.278
Why have you strung him along with you?

769
00:53:43.846 --> 00:53:45.046
What do you mean strung along?

770
00:53:45.305 --> 00:53:47.242
Are you calling me a bull
who can be tagged along anywhere?

771
00:53:47.266 --> 00:53:48.077
Forget that, where are the papers?

772
00:53:48.101 --> 00:53:49.184
Who's... what... papers?

773
00:53:49.768 --> 00:53:51.008
Papers for this white elephant.

774
00:53:51.478 --> 00:53:52.956
Papers of this property... my dear Uncle.

775
00:53:52.980 --> 00:53:56.358
Ok, so I've figured out
the entire list of all the alive...

776
00:53:57.025 --> 00:53:59.045
...and dead relatives, every little detail.

777
00:53:59.069 --> 00:54:00.069
That was point number 2.

778
00:54:00.654 --> 00:54:02.030
Point 1 is papers.

779
00:54:02.531 --> 00:54:03.716
Who asked you to jump the order?

780
00:54:03.740 --> 00:54:06.010
Point number 2 and then...

781
00:54:06.034 --> 00:54:08.179
It's been days Pandey ji...
You seem to have dropped out of nowhere.

782
00:54:08.203 --> 00:54:10.348
Ya... I guess it was time for me to.

783
00:54:10.372 --> 00:54:14.084
Come... come...

784
00:54:48.994 --> 00:54:55.000
Aah! This... point no.1.

785
00:54:55.417 --> 00:54:56.835
I wasn't there during the day.

786
00:54:57.586 --> 00:54:58.605
Nor me.

787
00:54:58.629 --> 00:54:59.939
But you were there, Mishra ji!

788
00:54:59.963 --> 00:55:01.608
But no one's ever
there during afternoons.

789
00:55:01.632 --> 00:55:04.194
Whoever that chap was,
must have been a lawyer.

790
00:55:04.218 --> 00:55:06.553
Must have been?
He was indeed a lawyer...

791
00:55:07.387 --> 00:55:09.223
People are so naive in this house.

792
00:55:09.473 --> 00:55:11.784
That chap had a black coat on his arm
and no one noticed... amazing!

793
00:55:11.808 --> 00:55:13.411
Hey don't throw your knowledge
around here... it's ok.

794
00:55:13.435 --> 00:55:14.603
I am throwing knowledge?

795
00:55:15.062 --> 00:55:17.123
A man in a black coat,
he came, he saw and he went.

796
00:55:17.147 --> 00:55:19.375
If you can apply your mind, so can I. OK?

797
00:55:19.399 --> 00:55:20.399
Look here now.

798
00:55:20.609 --> 00:55:23.028
Look... come here.

799
00:55:25.656 --> 00:55:27.032
This is the mansion.

800
00:55:27.658 --> 00:55:30.744
There is Mirza and then there is us.

801
00:55:31.119 --> 00:55:32.538
The tenants.

802
00:55:32.829 --> 00:55:37.268
Tenant Baankey... Dadda called
the archaeology department fellow.

803
00:55:37.292 --> 00:55:38.770
Hey... I never called anyone.

804
00:55:38.794 --> 00:55:41.022
Keep quiet! And don't interrupt now...
Guddo... you go on now, we're all ears.

805
00:55:41.046 --> 00:55:44.758
This archeology department chap
has met Mirza as well.

806
00:55:45.050 --> 00:55:48.095
And now Mirza has this
lawyer on his side too!!

807
00:55:49.471 --> 00:55:50.698
Let me tell you what's
really happening here.

808
00:55:50.722 --> 00:55:53.522
Archeology department, the lawyer
and Mirza, they're all on one side...

809
00:55:53.767 --> 00:55:55.286
...and we, tenants have no one on our side.

810
00:55:55.310 --> 00:55:57.038
What do you think I've been
trying explain for the longest time?

811
00:55:57.062 --> 00:55:59.231
So, don't try to explain...
get out of here, you!

812
00:56:00.023 --> 00:56:01.358
Very well!

813
00:56:02.109 --> 00:56:03.402
Can't we get our own lawyer?

814
00:56:03.735 --> 00:56:05.737
And how do you fathom
that will happen? For free?

815
00:56:05.988 --> 00:56:07.108
"Can't we get a lawyer" hah!

816
00:56:07.281 --> 00:56:08.383
Well... we can kiss
this mansion goodbye then.

817
00:56:08.407 --> 00:56:10.009
It's not that simple to chuck us out.

818
00:56:10.033 --> 00:56:11.803
Mirza's been at it... scheming
to chuck us out everyday...

819
00:56:11.827 --> 00:56:14.222
...and our man is living in
a fool's paradise.

820
00:56:14.246 --> 00:56:15.557
We've been living here for years, ok?!

821
00:56:15.581 --> 00:56:17.058
We been paying rent regularly,
with receipts.

822
00:56:17.082 --> 00:56:18.125
So what?

823
00:56:20.877 --> 00:56:22.629
Won't let the mansion go.

824
00:56:34.224 --> 00:56:37.161
As you can see, there's non stop digging
going on here for the past three days.

825
00:56:37.185 --> 00:56:39.122
If indeed 1000 tonnes
gold is found here...

826
00:56:39.146 --> 00:56:42.667
...today according to the saint's dream,
that will be India's...

827
00:56:42.691 --> 00:56:46.069
That's right... four meters to the left.

828
00:56:47.779 --> 00:56:51.742
Shukla ji... Shukla ji.
Increase the number of cranes...

829
00:56:53.201 --> 00:56:54.620
Shukla ji.

830
00:56:55.495 --> 00:56:57.914
What are you doing here?

831
00:56:59.249 --> 00:57:00.626
Wait there.

832
00:57:02.836 --> 00:57:03.896
Yes, tell me.

833
00:57:03.920 --> 00:57:06.524
- Mirza's gone wild.
- What do you mean?

834
00:57:06.548 --> 00:57:08.842
He's engaged a lawyer...
filed a case against us.

835
00:57:09.092 --> 00:57:11.928
- That mansion is as good as gone
- That property ain't going nowhere.

836
00:57:12.512 --> 00:57:13.847
He has no case.

837
00:57:14.181 --> 00:57:15.575
Needn't worry as long as I am here.
I am no loser.

838
00:57:15.599 --> 00:57:16.701
In fact I am the loser here.

839
00:57:16.725 --> 00:57:20.979
While I am taking you around Lucknow,
you are meeting Mirza in private.

840
00:57:22.105 --> 00:57:23.791
Oh come on... I'd met him once...
to survey the property...

841
00:57:23.815 --> 00:57:25.084
...and you bloody well know about that!

842
00:57:25.108 --> 00:57:26.961
So what was that lawyer
doing at the property then?

843
00:57:26.985 --> 00:57:28.320
Don't boil my blood!

844
00:57:29.404 --> 00:57:30.530
Look over there.

845
00:57:30.989 --> 00:57:34.109
Some random saint had a dream about a
1000 tonnes of gold that's buried here...

846
00:57:34.326 --> 00:57:35.845
...that's all it took to start
this manic digging.

847
00:57:35.869 --> 00:57:38.997
Gold? So that's the mad rush all about.

848
00:57:39.247 --> 00:57:40.582
Bullshit... There's nothing here.

849
00:57:40.832 --> 00:57:41.976
But I got to do my job.

850
00:57:42.000 --> 00:57:45.170
And do you see the media,
like hungry hyenas.

851
00:57:46.838 --> 00:57:48.024
Anyway... did you have a word
with the tenants?

852
00:57:48.048 --> 00:57:49.208
Just the way I'd told you to.

853
00:57:50.008 --> 00:57:50.944
No.

854
00:57:50.968 --> 00:57:52.928
For heaven's sake...
can you do that first...

855
00:57:53.428 --> 00:57:54.846
...and let me handle this lawyer.

856
00:57:57.140 --> 00:57:59.101
1000 tonnes of gold is a lot.

857
00:57:59.726 --> 00:58:01.144
And you're getting none of it.

858
00:58:10.987 --> 00:58:13.007
You look pretty... this way.

859
00:58:13.031 --> 00:58:13.966
I'll be back in minute.

860
00:58:13.990 --> 00:58:14.717
Where are you off to?

861
00:58:14.741 --> 00:58:15.741
I said I am coming.

862
00:58:16.118 --> 00:58:18.829
These papers are all I have.

863
00:58:25.836 --> 00:58:28.422
Alright... that's point no. 1: papers.

864
00:58:28.714 --> 00:58:29.191
Hmm.

865
00:58:29.215 --> 00:58:30.674
And now point no 2...

866
00:58:30.966 --> 00:58:32.944
...because your Begum
doesn't have a clear title...

867
00:58:32.968 --> 00:58:36.847
...you'll have to procure
NOC from her relatives.

868
00:58:38.390 --> 00:58:39.826
Where in the world will I find them...?

869
00:58:39.850 --> 00:58:43.979
Well, you'll have to... come what may...
are you getting me?

870
00:58:44.438 --> 00:58:46.358
'Cause if this property
is declared 'disputed'...

871
00:58:46.523 --> 00:58:49.563
...then no force on earth can stop that
archeology fellow from entering it...

872
00:58:50.152 --> 00:58:51.587
...and that's the end of your dream...

873
00:58:51.611 --> 00:58:54.281
...to become the sole owner of that place.

874
00:58:54.740 --> 00:58:56.742
Here... now for god sake
keep these papers safe.

875
00:59:05.542 --> 00:59:07.836
I've let you in today.

876
00:59:08.587 --> 00:59:10.507
If you ever come in after
the gates are locked...

877
00:59:10.839 --> 00:59:13.479
...you can jolly well spend the rest
of the night outside the gate.

878
00:59:13.759 --> 00:59:16.428
You know Mirza, you can't even
imagine where I've been today.

879
00:59:16.803 --> 00:59:17.803
Really?

880
00:59:19.222 --> 00:59:20.640
Where from?

881
00:59:21.933 --> 00:59:26.938
Unnaao... A thousand tonnes
of gold is buried there.

882
00:59:27.647 --> 00:59:29.566
Gold...?

883
00:59:29.941 --> 00:59:32.360
Yeah and they are digging it up there.

884
00:59:32.944 --> 00:59:34.821
It's a mad rush, unbelievable.

885
00:59:36.615 --> 00:59:38.384
Hold on...
hold on... where are you off to?

886
00:59:38.408 --> 00:59:42.054
Do you remember... 2 years back...

887
00:59:42.078 --> 00:59:44.039
...they found two vaults buried in
an old mansion?

888
00:59:44.331 --> 00:59:45.331
Yes...?

889
00:59:45.999 --> 00:59:47.751
This place right here is a mansion too.

890
00:59:48.794 --> 00:59:50.337
Old one at that.

891
00:59:52.422 --> 00:59:55.842
But you wouldn't ever
dig up your own home... would you?

892
00:59:56.134 --> 00:59:57.552
Obviously... not.

893
00:59:57.928 --> 00:59:59.971
So... that's what got me late.

894
01:00:34.381 --> 01:00:36.007
Put your ears to the ground.

895
01:00:36.925 --> 01:00:38.009
Can you hear it?

896
01:00:53.859 --> 01:00:54.860
Here.

897
01:00:56.778 --> 01:00:57.988
Can your hear it?

898
01:00:58.321 --> 01:01:00.365
Nothing?

899
01:01:05.120 --> 01:01:07.205
What... where?

900
01:01:14.963 --> 01:01:16.006
Found anything?

901
01:01:19.926 --> 01:01:21.511
Gold...

902
01:01:29.686 --> 01:01:31.479
Gold... gold.

903
01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:35.525
Huh...

904
01:01:37.986 --> 01:01:40.322
There's nothing inside... see.

905
01:02:01.718 --> 01:02:03.219
Greed... Mirza?

906
01:02:06.097 --> 01:02:07.724
Greed, is like slow poison.

907
01:02:08.808 --> 01:02:11.019
It eats up a person from inside.

908
01:02:13.939 --> 01:02:16.042
Look at yourself... lying on this cot...

909
01:02:16.066 --> 01:02:18.485
...in a year or two you'll find
yourself lying in a coffin...

910
01:02:18.777 --> 01:02:20.612
...if you don't stop this nonsense.

911
01:02:21.112 --> 01:02:22.822
The truth is...

912
01:02:24.407 --> 01:02:27.535
...firstly I haven't heard
of anyone dying of greed ever.

913
01:02:28.995 --> 01:02:33.083
Got it?
And secondly... I am not greedy.

914
01:02:33.625 --> 01:02:35.543
- You're not greedy?
- Not even an ounce.

915
01:02:36.086 --> 01:02:39.690
So this episode of digging up
for gold in the burning heat...

916
01:02:39.714 --> 01:02:41.314
...till you passed out, this behavior...

917
01:02:41.508 --> 01:02:42.818
Doesn't it amount to greed?

918
01:02:42.842 --> 01:02:48.741
You call that greed. I call it
my love for this mansion... immense love.

919
01:02:48.765 --> 01:02:50.141
Unparalleled love.

920
01:02:50.767 --> 01:02:52.686
And I can do anything for that love.

921
01:02:54.145 --> 01:02:58.817
Look, Begum's been keeping unwell,
and you've taken to this bed now...

922
01:02:59.985 --> 01:03:02.225
...have you ever thought of the future?
What will happen?

923
01:03:03.571 --> 01:03:04.174
When?

924
01:03:04.198 --> 01:03:07.492
You'll chuck us out, Begum's
not surviving another season...

925
01:03:07.909 --> 01:03:11.180
...who's going to look after you
and your dilapidated mansion?

926
01:03:11.204 --> 01:03:12.348
Have you ever thought about it?

927
01:03:12.372 --> 01:03:14.012
And you're not getting any younger at 78.

928
01:03:17.419 --> 01:03:18.795
Look at it this way.

929
01:03:19.045 --> 01:03:20.672
You have no kids.

930
01:03:21.214 --> 01:03:22.799
I have no father to look after.

931
01:03:23.383 --> 01:03:27.721
Forget the whole lawyer, court mess...
And adopt me.

932
01:03:30.682 --> 01:03:34.954
Get out of here... get out!

933
01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.455
Get out of here, you termite!

934
01:03:36.479 --> 01:03:38.165
I was giving some sound advice,
but you're not worth it.

935
01:03:38.189 --> 01:03:39.917
But don't you ever try to uproot me.

936
01:03:39.941 --> 01:03:42.360
I'm embedded here for good, got it?

937
01:03:42.819 --> 01:03:45.172
Adopt me... huh!
Get out, you parasite!

938
01:03:45.196 --> 01:03:46.489
Calls me a parasite, huh!!

939
01:03:46.823 --> 01:03:51.012
And that sheet... That's mine...
when did you sneak that in, huh?

940
01:03:51.036 --> 01:03:53.204
Your legendary crookery
...it'll never go away.

941
01:03:55.832 --> 01:03:57.417
Sure keep it... take it away.

942
01:03:57.709 --> 01:03:59.836
Just know that I've farted
on it the whole day.

943
01:04:05.050 --> 01:04:07.927
Why've you got us here Baankey...
and why are these cannons here?

944
01:04:09.846 --> 01:04:11.347
Because it's time now to attack.

945
01:04:11.598 --> 01:04:12.682
What do you mean...?

946
01:04:12.932 --> 01:04:14.601
Do you know who 'Asif-ud-daulla' was?

947
01:04:14.934 --> 01:04:17.695
C'mmon they're from Lucknow...
of course they would've heard his name.

948
01:04:17.812 --> 01:04:18.457
Of course.

949
01:04:18.481 --> 01:04:21.667
So Asifudaulla's mom
was quite a dominating lady...

950
01:04:21.691 --> 01:04:22.877
...she wouldn't let him be...

951
01:04:22.901 --> 01:04:25.504
...where he goes...
who he meets... plays with...

952
01:04:25.528 --> 01:04:27.798
...poor guy couldn't do
a thing without her approval...

953
01:04:27.822 --> 01:04:29.908
...then one day,
Asif-ud-daulla just lost it...

954
01:04:30.366 --> 01:04:31.802
...he said to hell with her
rules and regulations.

955
01:04:31.826 --> 01:04:33.137
I am going to Lucknow.

956
01:04:33.161 --> 01:04:37.207
He packed up his bags...
from Faizabad he moved to Lucknow...

957
01:04:37.749 --> 01:04:39.429
...and look what a beautiful city he made.

958
01:04:39.584 --> 01:04:41.044
And why are you telling us all this?

959
01:04:41.419 --> 01:04:44.380
'Cause Asif-ud-daulla's mom
and this Mirza in our lives...

960
01:04:44.839 --> 01:04:46.067
...they both are just the same.

961
01:04:46.091 --> 01:04:48.652
Don't dry the pickles in the sun...
don't park the car there.

962
01:04:48.676 --> 01:04:49.653
Why are the kids playing
in the courtyard...

963
01:04:49.677 --> 01:04:51.989
...mend the wall yourself...
I don't have the money for the painting...

964
01:04:52.013 --> 01:04:53.991
...if you come late
I won't let you in...

965
01:04:54.015 --> 01:04:56.559
...for god sake...
I'm done with his do's and don't's.

966
01:04:58.103 --> 01:05:00.063
Therefore, revolt!

967
01:05:02.065 --> 01:05:04.502
If that damn Haveli
doesn't have place for such gentle...

968
01:05:04.526 --> 01:05:06.569
...humble, peace loving tenants like us...

969
01:05:06.903 --> 01:05:08.423
...it certainly can't belong to Mirza.

970
01:05:08.488 --> 01:05:09.989
When did it ever belong to him?

971
01:05:10.615 --> 01:05:12.117
But why should we vacate this place?

972
01:05:12.408 --> 01:05:16.329
To enable the restoration work...
how will it happen otherwise?

973
01:05:16.996 --> 01:05:19.850
Once the restoration is done...

974
01:05:19.874 --> 01:05:23.002
...we'll request the ministry of art and
culture to commission a museum here...

975
01:05:23.795 --> 01:05:24.838
...a place in history.

976
01:05:26.673 --> 01:05:29.634
Sooner or later, we'll be served
a notice to vacate the house...

977
01:05:30.051 --> 01:05:32.011
...it's a matter of
heritage property now.

978
01:05:32.720 --> 01:05:33.906
But Shukla ji believes...

979
01:05:33.930 --> 01:05:36.367
...we could definitely get an allotment
for a LIG house as a compensation.

980
01:05:36.391 --> 01:05:37.911
That's if we go by Shukla ji's advice.

981
01:05:38.393 --> 01:05:40.395
The government is bound
to provide compensation...

982
01:05:40.770 --> 01:05:42.355
...where will you go otherwise...

983
01:05:42.814 --> 01:05:43.958
...in case it's proven
to be a heritage property.

984
01:05:43.982 --> 01:05:46.382
But its not proven yet,
so why are we jumping to conclusions?

985
01:05:47.735 --> 01:05:50.335
That's why I said, "in case",
if you didn't hear me correctly...

986
01:05:52.657 --> 01:05:54.537
...but we will prove it...
a heritage property.

987
01:05:55.034 --> 01:05:56.786
What if we need a MIG accommodation?

988
01:06:01.666 --> 01:06:03.793
We could try for one or two of them...

989
01:06:05.170 --> 01:06:07.422
...but even the LIG is pretty good too.

990
01:06:08.715 --> 01:06:11.009
There's a private toilet,
separate kitchen.

991
01:06:11.843 --> 01:06:14.095
Think about it, ok?

992
01:06:14.762 --> 01:06:15.865
Should we move ahead now?

993
01:06:15.889 --> 01:06:17.992
Have you ever thought about
this dilapidated mansion?

994
01:06:18.016 --> 01:06:19.535
What if it collapsed one day?

995
01:06:19.559 --> 01:06:21.912
Your bodies will have to be hauled
out with the help of cranes...

996
01:06:21.936 --> 01:06:23.188
...one limb at a time!

997
01:06:31.988 --> 01:06:33.757
We need to go to Sitapur.

998
01:06:33.781 --> 01:06:34.800
Take the bus headed from Qaisarbagh.

999
01:06:34.824 --> 01:06:35.801
From Qaisarbagh?

1000
01:06:35.825 --> 01:06:36.927
Let's go then... to Qaisarbagh.

1001
01:06:36.951 --> 01:06:40.163
Passengers for Sitapur,
please move to Qaisarbagh.

1002
01:06:40.872 --> 01:06:43.541
A powerful man will
dance on drum's beat...

1003
01:06:45.168 --> 01:06:47.879
...like a monkey of juggler
when life plays its music.

1004
01:06:49.589 --> 01:06:52.967
A powerful man will dance
on drum's beat...

1005
01:06:54.010 --> 01:06:57.013
...like a monkey of juggler
when life plays its music.

1006
01:06:58.264 --> 01:07:00.826
In the mint of breath...

1007
01:07:00.850 --> 01:07:02.411
- He's been in this state for 15 years now.
- ...limited coins will sound.

1008
01:07:02.435 --> 01:07:03.913
Get it done.
Everybody...

1009
01:07:03.937 --> 01:07:06.165
...is stuck in the fake
net of love and illusion.

1010
01:07:06.189 --> 01:07:08.918
- Fatto bi... She's still alive?
- Like Searching fresh...

1011
01:07:08.942 --> 01:07:11.545
- She refuses to die!
- ...water in the ocean

1012
01:07:11.569 --> 01:07:14.715
A powerful
man will dance on drums beat...

1013
01:07:14.739 --> 01:07:15.799
Should we?

1014
01:07:15.823 --> 01:07:18.368
...like a monkey of juggler
when life plays its music.

1015
01:07:19.702 --> 01:07:22.997
Would you know how to get to lane no 3?
A powerful man will dance on drums beat...

1016
01:07:23.623 --> 01:07:24.850
- You're here to meet Jamila bano?
- ...like a monkey of juggler

1017
01:07:24.874 --> 01:07:26.477
- Yes.
- When life plays its music.

1018
01:07:26.501 --> 01:07:27.981
She passed away... this very morning.

1019
01:07:29.837 --> 01:07:30.315
Passed away?

1020
01:07:30.339 --> 01:07:31.839
You're a wee bit late.

1021
01:07:32.090 --> 01:07:35.569
The funeral procession has left already...
if you wish I could drop you there.

1022
01:07:35.593 --> 01:07:36.844
Oh no... don't bother really...

1023
01:07:37.178 --> 01:07:38.846
- Are your sure?
- Yes yes, sure.

1024
01:07:39.973 --> 01:07:41.909
- She's gone!!
- Yes, she's gone.

1025
01:07:41.933 --> 01:07:42.661
This one too.

1026
01:07:42.685 --> 01:07:43.965
This case got solved on its own!

1027
01:07:46.437 --> 01:07:50.358
Luxury will have a cost.

1028
01:07:50.775 --> 01:07:55.405
A pipkin of timber
can be fired only once

1029
01:07:58.992 --> 01:08:01.744
We broke all relations with Fatima aunt...

1030
01:08:02.203 --> 01:08:04.998
...the day she married this Mirza.

1031
01:08:05.873 --> 01:08:08.918
We have nothing to do
with him or his mansion.

1032
01:08:09.335 --> 01:08:11.170
Now you get out from here...

1033
01:08:11.713 --> 01:08:14.775
...and never bother
showing your face to us.

1034
01:08:14.799 --> 01:08:17.218
When a spiritual soul encountered...

1035
01:08:17.510 --> 01:08:20.906
- Just put your thump here... right here ... thank you.
- ...powerful man will dance on drum's beat.

1036
01:08:20.930 --> 01:08:21.930
Mirza...

1037
01:08:23.891 --> 01:08:26.019
I've been wondering...
what just happened in there.

1038
01:08:27.854 --> 01:08:29.856
Why do these guys hate you so much?

1039
01:08:31.983 --> 01:08:33.026
Really?

1040
01:08:34.068 --> 01:08:35.748
- No...?
- I never felt anything like that.

1041
01:08:36.988 --> 01:08:38.072
- Really?
- No.

1042
01:08:40.158 --> 01:08:40.885
I must have misheard.

1043
01:08:40.909 --> 01:08:44.763
Like searching for
fresh water in the ocean.

1044
01:08:44.787 --> 01:08:48.124
A powerful man
will dance on drum's beat...

1045
01:08:49.667 --> 01:08:54.339
...like a monkey of juggler
when life plays its music.

1046
01:08:55.840 --> 01:08:57.050
Stop here.

1047
01:09:01.220 --> 01:09:02.347
Here.

1048
01:09:16.944 --> 01:09:19.822
Desire... it can make
a man stoop really low.

1049
01:09:21.991 --> 01:09:23.368
I've 3 wonderful kids.

1050
01:09:23.701 --> 01:09:25.995
Fulfilling relationship with the wife.

1051
01:09:26.954 --> 01:09:28.206
And yet?

1052
01:09:29.332 --> 01:09:30.958
I am here with you in this room.

1053
01:09:34.003 --> 01:09:38.108
I feel I may not be able to do this.

1054
01:09:38.132 --> 01:09:39.717
Hope you won't judge me.

1055
01:09:41.969 --> 01:09:42.970
No.

1056
01:09:44.514 --> 01:09:45.514
I get it.

1057
01:09:47.767 --> 01:09:49.787
I mean if your kids
ever come to know that...

1058
01:09:49.811 --> 01:09:51.663
...their dad is up to
all this hanky panky stuff.

1059
01:09:51.687 --> 01:09:53.207
Won't be the best situation to be, no?

1060
01:09:58.820 --> 01:09:59.821
A kiss?

1061
01:10:01.030 --> 01:10:02.030
Maybe just a kiss?

1062
01:10:02.824 --> 01:10:04.033
That will do no harm.

1063
01:10:09.163 --> 01:10:11.666
Uhh... there is an issue there as well.

1064
01:10:12.417 --> 01:10:13.709
Why?

1065
01:10:17.380 --> 01:10:22.051
Uh... It's embarrassing...
but... I have Pyorrhoea.

1066
01:10:27.765 --> 01:10:31.936
Ok... let's cut the crap...
and get straight to the point.

1067
01:10:32.979 --> 01:10:37.984
This file has all the documents...
my mark sheet etc.

1068
01:10:38.735 --> 01:10:41.154
You'd mentioned about
the museum right...

1069
01:10:41.779 --> 01:10:43.322
...I can take good care of it.

1070
01:10:43.906 --> 01:10:48.202
I mean you just get me a job
in your dept. now.

1071
01:10:49.120 --> 01:10:51.890
Alright... alright...
I'll take care of it... you needn't worry.

1072
01:10:51.914 --> 01:10:52.999
Alright then.

1073
01:10:53.624 --> 01:10:56.961
Ok listen...
whatever that happened here...

1074
01:10:59.255 --> 01:11:01.090
...just keep it to yourself.

1075
01:11:01.841 --> 01:11:03.009
Are you mad? Of course.

1076
01:11:03.426 --> 01:11:05.511
You just saved yourself
a lifetime of guilt.

1077
01:11:06.596 --> 01:11:07.680
Just a second.

1078
01:11:10.850 --> 01:11:11.910
Brick from the latrine wall.

1079
01:11:11.934 --> 01:11:13.728
You'd said you would
use it for the research?

1080
01:11:14.145 --> 01:11:15.813
Oh... of course... thanks.

1081
01:11:18.399 --> 01:11:19.293
Uh... may I?

1082
01:11:19.317 --> 01:11:19.901
Yeah?

1083
01:11:20.151 --> 01:11:21.861
Go see a dentist.

1084
01:11:29.202 --> 01:11:33.623
Remember the other day I'd come...
that's when I plucked these.

1085
01:11:34.540 --> 01:11:35.517
From the mango tree in our mansion...?

1086
01:11:35.541 --> 01:11:36.834
Put it down!

1087
01:11:38.002 --> 01:11:40.838
To prove the historical
status of the mansion...

1088
01:11:41.339 --> 01:11:42.757
...not to make pickles from them.

1089
01:11:43.007 --> 01:11:44.007
Come here.

1090
01:11:44.842 --> 01:11:45.134
Look at this.

1091
01:11:45.384 --> 01:11:45.885
Brick?

1092
01:11:46.260 --> 01:11:47.845
It's from your latrine.

1093
01:11:49.138 --> 01:11:51.158
So why is it kept on a plate?

1094
01:11:51.182 --> 01:11:55.144
We're researching on it...
its shape... size... width... length...

1095
01:11:55.394 --> 01:11:56.594
...the sand it's made up of...

1096
01:11:56.979 --> 01:11:58.339
...basically to determine its age.

1097
01:11:59.982 --> 01:12:01.817
You haven't studied at all... right?

1098
01:12:04.820 --> 01:12:05.905
As if we had the money.

1099
01:12:06.155 --> 01:12:07.657
Your dad died while he was young...?

1100
01:12:08.825 --> 01:12:13.538
Some years back.
I took over the wheat mill since grade six.

1101
01:12:13.955 --> 01:12:16.791
Mummy was adamant to teach Neetu,
Payal, Guddo...

1102
01:12:17.500 --> 01:12:19.710
...so and since then
I've been grinding...for them.

1103
01:12:20.795 --> 01:12:24.507
You are also sad... hmm.

1104
01:12:25.550 --> 01:12:27.790
You need to reach a conclusion soon...
with this brick...

1105
01:12:28.094 --> 01:12:30.072
...'cause I can sense danger
lurking all over the mansion.

1106
01:12:30.096 --> 01:12:32.866
Look mister... work will
happen at its own pace...

1107
01:12:32.890 --> 01:12:36.185
...alright... just be thankful
that I got you here in the lab.

1108
01:12:38.396 --> 01:12:39.689
And by the way.

1109
01:12:43.860 --> 01:12:45.820
Guddo is an intelligent girl.

1110
01:12:46.654 --> 01:12:48.573
I'll take care of her... job.

1111
01:13:00.626 --> 01:13:02.187
Hey... stop.

1112
01:13:02.211 --> 01:13:04.130
- Get me to the court quickly.
- Stop... hey.

1113
01:13:04.463 --> 01:13:05.691
You carry on... just carry on.

1114
01:13:05.715 --> 01:13:08.092
I said stop... hold on.

1115
01:13:10.011 --> 01:13:11.071
What's with you, dude?

1116
01:13:11.095 --> 01:13:11.823
What?

1117
01:13:11.847 --> 01:13:16.142
We don't need to be a lawyer
to know the legal rights of a tenant.

1118
01:13:16.517 --> 01:13:17.560
Got it?

1119
01:13:20.146 --> 01:13:21.986
- Fine... but I am... Mirza's lawyer.
- Really?

1120
01:13:23.149 --> 01:13:24.859
...And your bullying
won't work with me...

1121
01:13:25.985 --> 01:13:32.033
...'cause grabbing someone's land
or property is not only illegal...

1122
01:13:32.742 --> 01:13:34.076
...but also a punishable crime.

1123
01:13:34.327 --> 01:13:37.389
But where have we grabbed it?
We are paying the rent.

1124
01:13:37.413 --> 01:13:37.849
Ya!

1125
01:13:37.873 --> 01:13:38.998
You call that rent?

1126
01:13:39.498 --> 01:13:39.957
What else?!

1127
01:13:40.207 --> 01:13:40.977
It's pittance.

1128
01:13:41.001 --> 01:13:42.209
Look at me, Mr Pittance.

1129
01:13:42.585 --> 01:13:43.127
Mind your language.

1130
01:13:43.544 --> 01:13:45.630
Whatever it may be,
but we are still paying it...

1131
01:13:46.005 --> 01:13:48.174
...therefore we have right to privacy...

1132
01:13:48.841 --> 01:13:51.481
...you can't just walk in and
out of our home at unearthly hours...

1133
01:13:52.011 --> 01:13:55.115
...you can't cut our water or electricity supplies...
right to basic need...

1134
01:13:55.139 --> 01:13:57.159
...even if we don't pay
the rent for months...

1135
01:13:57.183 --> 01:13:59.953
...right to repair fund...who do you think
should get that wall mended?

1136
01:13:59.977 --> 01:14:01.913
And what about the plastering and painting
and other maintenance?

1137
01:14:01.937 --> 01:14:03.606
Should I list out more rights?

1138
01:14:04.106 --> 01:14:05.792
Sir, even we can file
a case against you...

1139
01:14:05.816 --> 01:14:07.794
...that of exploitation...alright...?

1140
01:14:07.818 --> 01:14:10.738
Madam, since you've clearly
researched all this...

1141
01:14:10.988 --> 01:14:14.367
...am sure you've also heard
of the rights of a landlord...

1142
01:14:14.742 --> 01:14:16.622
...the damaged wall
that you're talking about...

1143
01:14:16.869 --> 01:14:18.429
...who do you think did that damage...?

1144
01:14:18.954 --> 01:14:20.057
So if you know what I mean...

1145
01:14:20.081 --> 01:14:22.059
...a case of damage of property
can be filed against you...

1146
01:14:22.083 --> 01:14:23.894
...and in no time you'd be
thrown out of your home.

1147
01:14:23.918 --> 01:14:26.253
Thrown out... hah... my foot!

1148
01:14:27.129 --> 01:14:28.969
Well... I'd say go for
out of court settlement.

1149
01:14:29.548 --> 01:14:30.567
Everyone will benefit.

1150
01:14:30.591 --> 01:14:30.985
Let's go.

1151
01:14:31.009 --> 01:14:32.218
Hold on... hold on.

1152
01:14:32.760 --> 01:14:34.363
You don't teach us
our benefits and loss.

1153
01:14:34.387 --> 01:14:35.513
You mind your own damn life.

1154
01:14:35.888 --> 01:14:37.157
Get this, you can't exploit us...

1155
01:14:37.181 --> 01:14:38.224
...but if you try to...

1156
01:14:38.808 --> 01:14:42.019
...we know how to play
this game of 'sending notices'.

1157
01:14:42.395 --> 01:14:43.104
Now leave.

1158
01:14:43.396 --> 01:14:45.481
You slapped right on that lawyer's face!

1159
01:14:49.652 --> 01:14:50.736
She's too good.

1160
01:14:51.737 --> 01:14:54.031
Welcome welcome.

1161
01:14:56.909 --> 01:14:59.971
Old. Very old... mansion.

1162
01:14:59.995 --> 01:15:02.957
Click photo... photo... yes yes...
Come on... come over.

1163
01:15:04.583 --> 01:15:06.961
Be careful of the goat poop.

1164
01:15:07.628 --> 01:15:09.439
Look at this wall.

1165
01:15:09.463 --> 01:15:12.633
It's so thick...
this house is very old...

1166
01:15:12.967 --> 01:15:14.047
...over 100 years at least.

1167
01:15:14.176 --> 01:15:17.930
The landlord is a poor man...
see this architecture...

1168
01:15:18.723 --> 01:15:21.392
...English, French...
very meticulous in design...

1169
01:15:22.184 --> 01:15:23.078
...see these arcs.

1170
01:15:23.102 --> 01:15:24.102
Shukla ji?

1171
01:15:24.562 --> 01:15:29.316
Ok... you just take photos there...
there... click... go go go.

1172
01:15:29.817 --> 01:15:30.877
Where did you herd these tourists from?

1173
01:15:30.901 --> 01:15:32.820
Students from abroad.

1174
01:15:33.070 --> 01:15:35.781
China, Hong Kong, Cambodia...
research, architecture students.

1175
01:15:36.031 --> 01:15:42.347
So you've invaded my house yet again,
without my permission.

1176
01:15:42.371 --> 01:15:45.040
It's an official visit.
Need to investigate.

1177
01:15:45.374 --> 01:15:46.000
Investigate?

1178
01:15:46.333 --> 01:15:47.543
Come... come... keep walking.

1179
01:15:47.793 --> 01:15:51.857
This old man thinks that government
is interfering his house.

1180
01:15:51.881 --> 01:15:53.090
But he does not know.

1181
01:15:53.632 --> 01:15:57.946
Very soon this house will
be declared national property.

1182
01:15:57.970 --> 01:15:59.054
Awwwww.

1183
01:15:59.889 --> 01:16:01.432
You go there... click there.

1184
01:16:03.017 --> 01:16:04.657
Do you even know how old this mansion is?

1185
01:16:04.894 --> 01:16:06.103
How many years back... huh?

1186
01:16:07.021 --> 01:16:08.081
Can't say... not very old.

1187
01:16:08.105 --> 01:16:12.651
Go on write it down... under the heading heritage,
approximately 100 years old.

1188
01:16:14.070 --> 01:16:15.390
It's definitely lesser than that.

1189
01:16:16.030 --> 01:16:18.008
The walls haven't been white washed...
That's why.

1190
01:16:18.032 --> 01:16:21.577
Don't act smart with me now...
this is for government records.

1191
01:16:22.077 --> 01:16:23.397
When did this railing break away?

1192
01:16:23.621 --> 01:16:24.973
Maybe a year or two back.

1193
01:16:24.997 --> 01:16:26.123
He is lying.

1194
01:16:26.582 --> 01:16:28.685
Outright... it's been in that
broken state since I was born.

1195
01:16:28.709 --> 01:16:29.645
I am lying?

1196
01:16:29.669 --> 01:16:33.839
Write it down... 50 years back.

1197
01:16:39.220 --> 01:16:40.513
Come... come.

1198
01:16:40.846 --> 01:16:42.991
And this whole area
belongs to Begum.

1199
01:16:43.015 --> 01:16:44.910
All of this...
include it in the antique items list.

1200
01:16:44.934 --> 01:16:45.870
Click photos of each
one of them... come on.

1201
01:16:45.894 --> 01:16:47.204
There's more trash
stored inside as well.

1202
01:16:47.228 --> 01:16:48.228
Really?

1203
01:16:48.354 --> 01:16:51.357
Trash... what trash... huh?
Listen now.

1204
01:16:51.607 --> 01:16:53.877
Enough of this nonsense...
out from here now... out!

1205
01:16:53.901 --> 01:16:56.963
Yes yes we are leaving.

1206
01:16:56.987 --> 01:16:58.799
Yes, leave now!

1207
01:16:58.823 --> 01:17:00.032
I am warning you!

1208
01:17:00.407 --> 01:17:00.927
Mirza!

1209
01:17:00.951 --> 01:17:01.968
Get out! Leave now.

1210
01:17:01.992 --> 01:17:03.804
I am warning you...
don't you touch me... Mirza.

1211
01:17:03.828 --> 01:17:04.805
Hah! Don't touch me, he says.

1212
01:17:04.829 --> 01:17:05.972
I will get an official
letter the next time.

1213
01:17:05.996 --> 01:17:07.356
What letter are you talking about?

1214
01:17:07.540 --> 01:17:10.101
And how and with who's permission
are you selling this mansion?

1215
01:17:10.125 --> 01:17:11.812
- What do you mean?
- Selling it off... really?

1216
01:17:11.836 --> 01:17:13.021
Up until yesterday,
you were conniving with...

1217
01:17:13.045 --> 01:17:14.356
...the lawyer and filing
a case against us tenants...

1218
01:17:14.380 --> 01:17:15.982
- ...now you're selling it off?!
- Oh hold on... he can't sell.

1219
01:17:16.006 --> 01:17:19.444
It's my mansion my land, my will...

1220
01:17:19.468 --> 01:17:21.029
...I'll sell it as I wish, whosoever to...

1221
01:17:21.053 --> 01:17:23.156
You can, but not without our permission.

1222
01:17:23.180 --> 01:17:24.991
Permission... what permission,
what's this permission nonsense.

1223
01:17:25.015 --> 01:17:27.560
Permission... which I will never grant.

1224
01:17:27.852 --> 01:17:29.019
What do you mean?

1225
01:17:30.020 --> 01:17:31.020
Let the fun begin!

1226
01:17:37.903 --> 01:17:38.903
Permission.

1227
01:17:39.655 --> 01:17:40.735
Won't give permission! Huh!

1228
01:17:40.990 --> 01:17:41.615
Mansion...

1229
01:17:41.866 --> 01:17:42.968
That's one good thing you did...

1230
01:17:42.992 --> 01:17:45.095
...letting Gyanesh know that
you're selling the property.

1231
01:17:45.119 --> 01:17:45.721
Sit.

1232
01:17:45.745 --> 01:17:49.790
I just said what I had to at that point...

1233
01:17:50.374 --> 01:17:53.687
...but in reality...
I don't want to sell the mansion.

1234
01:17:53.711 --> 01:17:57.089
Firstly, we need a power of attorney
in your name.

1235
01:17:57.840 --> 01:18:01.594
For that we'll need Begum's
signature or a thumb impression.

1236
01:18:02.970 --> 01:18:05.848
I don't think she will be able
to recollect her signature...

1237
01:18:07.558 --> 01:18:08.976
...thumb impression.

1238
01:18:09.435 --> 01:18:12.956
That I'll ensure... but after that,
the mansion will be in my name, right?

1239
01:18:12.980 --> 01:18:17.610
Of course... mansion will be yours,
but only after Begum's death.

1240
01:18:18.652 --> 01:18:20.881
Here... get her signature
here at the bottom.

1241
01:18:20.905 --> 01:18:22.615
...or else her thumb
impression for sure.

1242
01:18:23.490 --> 01:18:24.093
Ok.

1243
01:18:24.117 --> 01:18:26.410
- Mirza, tea?
- No, you carry on.

1244
01:19:41.986 --> 01:19:45.280
Look at this mess?

1245
01:19:48.701 --> 01:19:50.244
It's on all my fingers.

1246
01:19:51.078 --> 01:19:52.663
But not this hand?

1247
01:19:53.038 --> 01:19:55.916
Don't worry...
we'll wash it... do you want some tea?

1248
01:20:11.974 --> 01:20:13.308
- What's this?
- Huh?

1249
01:20:14.143 --> 01:20:16.812
The thumb print you asked for...
what else?

1250
01:20:18.147 --> 01:20:19.189
It's all wrong.

1251
01:20:21.066 --> 01:20:22.585
I asked you to get a
left hand thumb impression...

1252
01:20:22.609 --> 01:20:23.929
...you've got the right hand one!

1253
01:20:25.904 --> 01:20:27.090
What's wrong now?

1254
01:20:27.114 --> 01:20:28.198
Am ok...

1255
01:20:29.742 --> 01:20:30.636
Am ok.

1256
01:20:30.660 --> 01:20:32.460
If the power of attorney
papers aren't done...

1257
01:20:34.496 --> 01:20:36.256
...you can forget about
your beloved mansion.

1258
01:20:48.302 --> 01:20:49.928
Here comes Mirza.

1259
01:20:57.311 --> 01:20:59.021
How are you, Begum?

1260
01:21:26.632 --> 01:21:28.008
It's ok.

1261
01:21:43.398 --> 01:21:45.859
Like I was saying...

1262
01:21:46.151 --> 01:21:50.739
...let bygones be bygones...

1263
01:21:51.240 --> 01:21:58.080
...we'll leave things the way
they were... like always...

1264
01:21:58.664 --> 01:22:01.875
Baankey can stay...

1265
01:22:02.126 --> 01:22:06.338
...I can talk to Christopher...
he will withdraw the case and sir...

1266
01:22:06.922 --> 01:22:13.095
...all the investigations
that you're conducting...

1267
01:22:13.387 --> 01:22:15.156
...all that can also stop... what say...?

1268
01:22:15.180 --> 01:22:21.061
Look Mirza,
this ship has now sailed too far...

1269
01:22:22.187 --> 01:22:24.857
...the mansion has been
documented in our records...

1270
01:22:25.190 --> 01:22:26.470
...and there is no turning back.

1271
01:22:26.775 --> 01:22:27.985
Oh... but.

1272
01:22:29.695 --> 01:22:31.631
- Let me show you something.
- Huh?

1273
01:22:31.655 --> 01:22:33.341
You should see how
our department works...

1274
01:22:33.365 --> 01:22:34.658
...you will feel proud too.

1275
01:22:36.034 --> 01:22:38.162
This is our lab.

1276
01:22:38.704 --> 01:22:41.039
Everything is done
very meticulously here...

1277
01:22:41.665 --> 01:22:44.376
...with minute detailing...
all these are antiques.

1278
01:22:48.463 --> 01:22:51.467
Do you have an idea how much
it costs in London... America?

1279
01:22:52.050 --> 01:22:54.654
Yes... all that is fine
but what about my mansion?

1280
01:22:54.678 --> 01:22:56.558
Again that mansion!
That's all you can think of.

1281
01:22:57.097 --> 01:22:58.658
Do you know how
much that mansion costs?

1282
01:22:58.682 --> 01:23:00.559
You'll lose your sense... if I tell you.

1283
01:23:01.894 --> 01:23:04.038
No... I mean... I don't know... how much?
How much do you think it's worth?

1284
01:23:04.062 --> 01:23:07.232
Its worth... it's priceless!

1285
01:23:10.319 --> 01:23:12.362
But... Its monetary value?

1286
01:23:13.363 --> 01:23:15.032
Priceless.

1287
01:23:16.408 --> 01:23:17.451
Uh... oh...?

1288
01:23:18.952 --> 01:23:19.952
Come.

1289
01:23:20.120 --> 01:23:25.042
Some things in life are so invaluable that
you cannot put a number to their worth...

1290
01:23:25.375 --> 01:23:27.669
...for eg. a mother's love...

1291
01:23:29.296 --> 01:23:31.089
Begum's love... in your case...

1292
01:23:31.924 --> 01:23:37.137
How invaluable it is...
but can you put a number to it?!

1293
01:23:38.263 --> 01:23:42.768
Similarly, your mansion...
priceless.

1294
01:23:43.227 --> 01:23:48.124
Oh no no no... hold on, hold on.

1295
01:23:48.148 --> 01:23:53.946
I am ok... uh... don't worry... am ok.

1296
01:23:54.905 --> 01:23:57.258
- What did you say... priceless?
- Yes... absolutely priceless.

1297
01:23:57.282 --> 01:23:59.636
So what's his problem if I went
and met that lawyer, Christopher?

1298
01:23:59.660 --> 01:24:02.300
Why is he creating such a ruckus...
and it's not that I went alone.

1299
01:24:02.537 --> 01:24:04.289
Alone? Didn't you go alone
to meet Gyanesh?!

1300
01:24:05.457 --> 01:24:07.602
Since the day she's
stopped oiling her hair...

1301
01:24:07.626 --> 01:24:09.729
...it's evident what all is
she up to...it's all clear.

1302
01:24:09.753 --> 01:24:12.047
- Baankey... I'm coming over.
- Hmm

1303
01:24:12.923 --> 01:24:14.275
Not that anyone's complaining about you...

1304
01:24:14.299 --> 01:24:15.902
...but you've been acting
footloose nowadays.

1305
01:24:15.926 --> 01:24:16.903
I don't care.

1306
01:24:16.927 --> 01:24:18.727
...I'd gone to get a job done...
that's all...

1307
01:24:19.012 --> 01:24:21.306
Exactly my point...
why are you meddling in between?

1308
01:24:21.723 --> 01:24:23.034
Why are you interfering?

1309
01:24:23.058 --> 01:24:25.245
'Cause I don't think you're capable
of doing this by yourself.

1310
01:24:25.269 --> 01:24:27.497
All you're doing is being
Gyanesh's lapdog...

1311
01:24:27.521 --> 01:24:28.498
...he promised an LIG flat
and you fell for it...

1312
01:24:28.522 --> 01:24:32.109
...while I'm talking about a proper flat...
if not here... then a backup.

1313
01:24:32.359 --> 01:24:34.403
Well... Guddo's making sense.

1314
01:24:34.653 --> 01:24:36.613
Ok then! Listen to her.

1315
01:24:36.905 --> 01:24:39.384
I am out of this, mom...
Don't come to me for anything.

1316
01:24:39.408 --> 01:24:42.095
Just look at him, mom...
look at him... he's just jealous.

1317
01:24:42.119 --> 01:24:44.538
Truth is he can't handle
the fact that I have gone and...

1318
01:24:44.788 --> 01:24:46.348
...done something productive on my own.

1319
01:24:46.540 --> 01:24:49.501
Brother... you go ahead and do your
own thing... I'll manage everything...

1320
01:24:49.751 --> 01:24:51.521
...mom, the house
and these two as well...

1321
01:24:51.545 --> 01:24:53.225
...you can just go
and romance that Fauzia.

1322
01:24:53.714 --> 01:24:55.090
Who's this Fauzia now?

1323
01:24:57.092 --> 01:24:58.152
No one... just don't bother.

1324
01:24:58.176 --> 01:24:59.416
Are you getting married to her?

1325
01:24:59.761 --> 01:25:03.432
Brother, you can romance
Fauzia on the terrace.

1326
01:25:04.266 --> 01:25:07.102
Just like Guddo... she romances
many boys behind the water tank.

1327
01:25:10.272 --> 01:25:11.272
Guddo?

1328
01:25:17.112 --> 01:25:22.200
What happened? Begum? She's not well?

1329
01:25:32.502 --> 01:25:37.049
Uh... well... You look somewhat sad?

1330
01:25:38.258 --> 01:25:39.618
Can't say anything at this moment.

1331
01:25:39.760 --> 01:25:42.346
She's not going to make it, is it?

1332
01:25:43.221 --> 01:25:45.891
Or...?

1333
01:25:46.350 --> 01:25:48.060
Can't say anything at this moment.

1334
01:25:49.353 --> 01:25:52.189
The disease is such that...
everything is...

1335
01:25:53.023 --> 01:25:54.024
So it's time for...?

1336
01:25:57.069 --> 01:25:58.429
Can't say anything at this moment.

1337
01:25:59.446 --> 01:26:02.383
- You should be prepared...
- No... no I get it... I understand.

1338
01:26:02.407 --> 01:26:04.159
- My fees?
- Fees?

1339
01:26:06.078 --> 01:26:09.956
That's all I have on me...
you may leave.

1340
01:26:14.711 --> 01:26:15.754
Hey... who got him here?

1341
01:26:16.004 --> 01:26:17.982
- No... no you go inside.
- Why did you get him here?

1342
01:26:18.006 --> 01:26:20.985
- Go inside... to Begum.
- How did you just walk in like that?

1343
01:26:21.009 --> 01:26:22.569
Why don't you go inside to the Begum...

1344
01:26:22.886 --> 01:26:24.221
Oh... I see.

1345
01:26:24.721 --> 01:26:29.101
You can't see her
in so much pain... hmm.

1346
01:26:29.351 --> 01:26:32.854
- Get him out of here.
- I swear you're worse than a devil.

1347
01:26:34.106 --> 01:26:38.860
Don't call me that... I'm no devil...
I'm telling you again, ok?

1348
01:26:41.071 --> 01:26:42.697
Get out of my way.

1349
01:27:08.098 --> 01:27:09.307
So Mirza... tell me.

1350
01:27:09.724 --> 01:27:11.244
I need a shroud.

1351
01:27:11.268 --> 01:27:12.537
- Shroud?
- Yesss...

1352
01:27:12.561 --> 01:27:15.355
- Is it the Begum?
- Why don't you show me one huh?

1353
01:27:18.150 --> 01:27:19.151
When did she pass away?

1354
01:27:20.902 --> 01:27:23.172
- How much is it for?
- Rs.150...

1355
01:27:23.196 --> 01:27:26.050
Can you show me something cheaper?

1356
01:27:26.074 --> 01:27:30.370
Mirza... have a little shame... huh?
You can't be negotiating at this hour?

1357
01:27:35.459 --> 01:27:37.878
Here... take it, that's all I have.

1358
01:27:38.295 --> 01:27:39.772
Why are you packing so many flowers?

1359
01:27:39.796 --> 01:27:42.048
I'm not decorating my house...
here keep them back.

1360
01:27:50.807 --> 01:27:53.143
That far... huh?

1361
01:27:54.394 --> 01:27:58.190
Begum's mother, her dad...
they're all buried in the mansion.

1362
01:27:58.857 --> 01:28:00.177
And you want to burry Begum here?

1363
01:28:01.026 --> 01:28:06.865
The farther she is from the mansion...
the better...

1364
01:28:07.115 --> 01:28:10.994
...she'll fit in this little space.

1365
01:28:12.078 --> 01:28:16.082
Even after she's dead...
if she remains stuck in the mansion...

1366
01:28:16.625 --> 01:28:17.709
...what's the point then?

1367
01:28:18.168 --> 01:28:19.336
But you'll have to pay.

1368
01:28:19.878 --> 01:28:24.758
Hmm... you get the ground ready...
I'm getting her here.

1369
01:28:25.550 --> 01:28:28.011
I'll pay you then... now move.

1370
01:28:38.063 --> 01:28:40.333
You're looking beautiful
Begum... come... quick.

1371
01:28:40.357 --> 01:28:43.044
Begum} Thanks,
I'm seeing you after many days myself.

1372
01:28:43.068 --> 01:28:45.362
Dulhain} Come this way, Begum.

1373
01:28:45.862 --> 01:28:48.448
Oh! This vulture is back?

1374
01:28:54.079 --> 01:28:55.056
Where to?

1375
01:28:55.080 --> 01:28:58.160
She's been really beat because of her illness...
I'll take her out for a walk.

1376
01:28:58.500 --> 01:29:00.460
We'll also look up the doctor
on our way back... I

1377
01:29:02.170 --> 01:29:03.463
Let me look for tempo.

1378
01:29:03.797 --> 01:29:06.049
- Go quickly... and look for one.
- Yes yes.

1379
01:29:16.893 --> 01:29:18.019
Let's go.

1380
01:30:23.668 --> 01:30:27.189
Our Begum... she really cares for you.

1381
01:30:27.213 --> 01:30:29.549
She's got your favourite
cotton candy... try some.

1382
01:30:34.137 --> 01:30:37.223
Have it... and go to sleep now.

1383
01:31:15.720 --> 01:31:17.639
- So here is the blueprint.
- Blueprint.

1384
01:31:18.139 --> 01:31:21.619
It's a fifteen floor building...
12 floors here and 3 on this side.

1385
01:31:21.643 --> 01:31:22.995
They'll all be next to each other?

1386
01:31:23.019 --> 01:31:24.955
Yes next to each other
but 12 floors tall!!

1387
01:31:24.979 --> 01:31:26.666
Mirza's here!!! What should I do?

1388
01:31:26.690 --> 01:31:28.084
- Sit, keep seated.
- Should I leave?

1389
01:31:28.108 --> 01:31:31.027
You've been appointed, my dear.

1390
01:31:31.903 --> 01:31:34.447
Come Mirza... come join us.

1391
01:31:35.115 --> 01:31:36.258
Her? She's Guddo.

1392
01:31:36.282 --> 01:31:37.701
Why have you called her?

1393
01:31:38.034 --> 01:31:40.495
She is an expert in legal language.

1394
01:31:41.079 --> 01:31:43.456
I've kept her as my assistant.
Come and sit.

1395
01:31:43.707 --> 01:31:45.041
Look at this... is it alright?

1396
01:31:45.792 --> 01:31:46.792
Very good.

1397
01:31:47.335 --> 01:31:49.003
Correct. Sit.

1398
01:31:50.046 --> 01:31:51.046
She's very helpful.

1399
01:31:54.759 --> 01:31:57.387
We've solved the case.

1400
01:31:59.013 --> 01:32:03.143
Look Guddo, the real villain
in your life is not Mirza...

1401
01:32:03.560 --> 01:32:07.147
...and Mirza,
your tenants aren't the villains either.

1402
01:32:08.022 --> 01:32:12.461
It's that conniving, meddling...
Gyanesh from archaeology

1403
01:32:12.485 --> 01:32:13.737
And what's the logic here?

1404
01:32:14.112 --> 01:32:15.113
What do you mean?

1405
01:32:17.157 --> 01:32:19.701
If this case reaches the civil court...

1406
01:32:20.034 --> 01:32:21.762
...it will take at least
6 to 8 months to resolve.

1407
01:32:21.786 --> 01:32:25.165
So the longer it drags...
The longer we can stay, isn't it?

1408
01:32:25.707 --> 01:32:27.542
Common Guddo, you should know better.

1409
01:32:28.126 --> 01:32:31.004
Gyanesh has his personal
interest in the mansion...

1410
01:32:31.588 --> 01:32:33.965
...that's why he is chasing this issue...

1411
01:32:34.215 --> 01:32:36.318
...the day he gets his hands
on some solid evidence...

1412
01:32:36.342 --> 01:32:38.862
...2 months is all it will
take... and you will be thrown out...

1413
01:32:38.887 --> 01:32:40.138
- 2 months... that's all?
- 2.

1414
01:32:41.347 --> 01:32:42.390
Ohh!

1415
01:32:42.932 --> 01:32:44.252
So Mirza...
I have a suggestion...

1416
01:32:46.728 --> 01:32:48.188
...before Gyanesh makes his move...

1417
01:32:50.106 --> 01:32:51.466
...there's only one option left...

1418
01:32:52.901 --> 01:32:53.902
...just sell the mansion.

1419
01:32:57.655 --> 01:33:00.241
- Hmm... I get it now.
- What?

1420
01:33:01.451 --> 01:33:04.245
If we sell the mansion,
we'll get something in hand...

1421
01:33:04.621 --> 01:33:06.348
...and if the government
takes over... we'll get zilch.

1422
01:33:06.372 --> 01:33:07.540
Correct!

1423
01:33:07.916 --> 01:33:08.916
You got it!

1424
01:33:09.000 --> 01:33:12.128
You know that builder... Mun Mun ji.

1425
01:33:12.378 --> 01:33:14.523
He's shown a lot of interest...
in the mansion... I know him personally.

1426
01:33:14.547 --> 01:33:16.317
We'll sort everything in a week or two.

1427
01:33:16.341 --> 01:33:18.927
I've spoken to him personally...
he's a very famous builder.

1428
01:33:19.469 --> 01:33:22.555
Gyanesh... that crook won't
last in front of him... am telling you.

1429
01:33:23.097 --> 01:33:23.807
Have you understood?

1430
01:33:24.098 --> 01:33:27.894
Have you got the papers now...
or you just sauntered in aimlessly?

1431
01:33:30.605 --> 01:33:32.124
What about the money...
when can we get that?

1432
01:33:32.148 --> 01:33:34.084
Can you get the papers in place first?

1433
01:33:34.108 --> 01:33:36.420
This isn't a flea market...
we're not selling trinkets here.

1434
01:33:36.444 --> 01:33:38.214
- Guddo?
- One second.

1435
01:33:38.238 --> 01:33:40.341
Really Mirza...
your status is no less than a beggar.

1436
01:33:40.365 --> 01:33:41.842
No illegal talking please.

1437
01:33:41.866 --> 01:33:44.970
We're talking about millions here.

1438
01:33:44.994 --> 01:33:47.514
We must have a proper deal in place...
I am very clear about it.

1439
01:33:48.414 --> 01:33:51.125
Ok... ok... ok.

1440
01:33:51.501 --> 01:33:52.794
Thank you.

1441
01:33:53.378 --> 01:33:56.631
Guddo, file these duplicates please.

1442
01:34:02.929 --> 01:34:06.182
Hello hello... yes... Sinha you bugger,
why is it taking so much time?

1443
01:34:06.683 --> 01:34:09.435
Uncle... few formalities are left.

1444
01:34:09.811 --> 01:34:12.689
You can consider it done...
Gyanesh... tell him.

1445
01:34:13.106 --> 01:34:16.418
Uncle it's like this... the bricks of
the mansion aren't exactly...

1446
01:34:16.442 --> 01:34:18.128
...the pristine antique ones like in
the historical Imambara...

1447
01:34:18.152 --> 01:34:25.135
...but I can tell you that it's the
typical British / French structure ones...

1448
01:34:25.159 --> 01:34:28.538
...matches perfectly with it...about 20%.

1449
01:34:28.913 --> 01:34:31.684
So it's done then...
go get the report ready.

1450
01:34:31.708 --> 01:34:33.334
Just one more thing, Uncle.

1451
01:34:33.710 --> 01:34:37.398
There's an old mango tree there...
we're in talks with the forest dept...

1452
01:34:37.422 --> 01:34:39.775
...we're figuring out its age...
the variety of the plant?

1453
01:34:39.799 --> 01:34:44.387
Even the mango tree is witness to the
historical importance of the mansion...

1454
01:34:45.054 --> 01:34:46.699
...then why are we dithering so much, Sinha?

1455
01:34:46.723 --> 01:34:48.163
Look, I am not in power right now...

1456
01:34:48.349 --> 01:34:50.160
...so no media's going to
really pay attention to me...

1457
01:34:50.184 --> 01:34:51.477
...let's wrap this up quickly...

1458
01:34:52.020 --> 01:34:53.730
- What date is it today?
- 29th.

1459
01:34:55.607 --> 01:34:58.687
Great... so let's get this sorted by
15th august... get the property sealed...

1460
01:34:59.027 --> 01:35:00.778
...and it should be livable
in about a year.

1461
01:35:01.029 --> 01:35:03.114
Uncle... you plan to...
stay in the mansion?

1462
01:35:04.115 --> 01:35:07.428
Who's this chap?
And why is he calling me uncle?

1463
01:35:07.452 --> 01:35:09.892
That mansion has a lot of tenants..
Uncle... he's one of them.

1464
01:35:10.121 --> 01:35:11.164
Alright... ok.

1465
01:35:11.497 --> 01:35:13.297
Give him some space
in the servant quarters...

1466
01:35:13.333 --> 01:35:15.060
...that are being constructed
behind the mansion.

1467
01:35:15.084 --> 01:35:16.084
- Alright.
- Ok.

1468
01:35:16.294 --> 01:35:17.294
See you.

1469
01:35:22.467 --> 01:35:25.154
Get the bricks tested
in the lab... real quick.

1470
01:35:25.178 --> 01:35:27.096
Alright... got it.

1471
01:35:27.639 --> 01:35:29.439
I'm not going to stay
in the servant quarters.

1472
01:35:29.724 --> 01:35:31.368
Listen you... just accept
what you're being offered...

1473
01:35:31.392 --> 01:35:33.645
...else you'll end up
with nothing at all.

1474
01:35:33.937 --> 01:35:36.064
These are called the LIG flats!

1475
01:35:51.079 --> 01:35:53.098
- Sir is busy.
- You can go in now.

1476
01:35:53.122 --> 01:35:54.122
Ok.

1477
01:35:59.671 --> 01:36:04.676
North facing and south...
they're both equally.

1478
01:36:05.343 --> 01:36:09.073
This better not be a bogus case
like the last time?

1479
01:36:09.097 --> 01:36:12.201
Not at all... this time we've got
all the papers in place...

1480
01:36:12.225 --> 01:36:13.985
...there's a duplicate copy...
right outside.

1481
01:36:14.185 --> 01:36:15.537
Do you need any help... kidnapping?

1482
01:36:15.561 --> 01:36:16.561
No... no no.

1483
01:36:16.938 --> 01:36:18.648
- Need goons?
- Not required...

1484
01:36:19.065 --> 01:36:23.152
You know the Begum...
she won't be around for too long.

1485
01:36:23.653 --> 01:36:26.864
And then Mirza... he's a dimwit...
the one sitting outside.

1486
01:36:27.115 --> 01:36:28.491
Mirza's sitting outside?

1487
01:36:29.075 --> 01:36:31.244
What's with you?
Get up and sit properly.

1488
01:36:33.121 --> 01:36:34.455
When is the deal happening...?

1489
01:36:35.373 --> 01:36:36.642
Max... Two to three days.

1490
01:36:36.666 --> 01:36:37.792
Let's do it in two days.

1491
01:36:38.126 --> 01:36:39.627
2 days... sounds doable.

1492
01:36:41.045 --> 01:36:42.755
What about my commission?

1493
01:36:43.715 --> 01:36:45.155
Just shut up... commission, my foot.

1494
01:36:53.808 --> 01:36:56.185
Mun Mun ji...
he maybe a big shot builder.

1495
01:36:57.020 --> 01:36:59.897
But am no less... I told him very clearly...
Mirza is my closest buddy.

1496
01:37:00.481 --> 01:37:02.150
I won't take him for a ride.

1497
01:37:02.483 --> 01:37:03.711
He asked me what should we do?

1498
01:37:03.735 --> 01:37:05.170
I told him to organise
the advance quickly.

1499
01:37:05.194 --> 01:37:06.696
Now?, he asked.

1500
01:37:07.280 --> 01:37:08.406
He really respects me.

1501
01:37:08.781 --> 01:37:10.092
I said take your time.

1502
01:37:10.116 --> 01:37:13.286
The moment Mirza hands over the
original papers... you pay the advance.

1503
01:37:14.120 --> 01:37:17.498
Now, you get the original papers,
as soon as you can.

1504
01:37:17.999 --> 01:37:19.208
I'll organise the bulldozer.

1505
01:37:19.751 --> 01:37:22.128
Like Now? Where will we go?

1506
01:37:23.254 --> 01:37:26.758
Not like right now Ms. Guddo...
Let's first get the advance.

1507
01:37:27.675 --> 01:37:30.261
- How much money will I get?
- 5% share.

1508
01:37:30.595 --> 01:37:31.929
How much would that be?

1509
01:37:32.180 --> 01:37:33.514
Rs, 500,000/-

1510
01:37:34.098 --> 01:37:35.892
Get the papers ready...

1511
01:37:36.434 --> 01:37:38.686
I'll begin at my end too.

1512
01:37:40.104 --> 01:37:41.206
Come on, Guddo.

1513
01:37:41.230 --> 01:37:44.734
Mirza... you're forgetting your file.

1514
01:37:45.068 --> 01:37:52.533
One... ten... hundred... thousand...
one hundred thousand.

1515
01:37:53.868 --> 01:37:57.371
Five hundred thousand!!!

1516
01:37:59.707 --> 01:38:00.907
That's five hundred thousand?!

1517
01:38:01.084 --> 01:38:03.312
Mirza... are you alright?

1518
01:38:03.336 --> 01:38:05.088
Huh?...one...

1519
01:38:05.505 --> 01:38:06.857
Should we drop you home?

1520
01:38:06.881 --> 01:38:08.132
Ten... Hundred...

1521
01:38:10.051 --> 01:38:12.929
Five hundred thousand!

1522
01:38:14.055 --> 01:38:18.285
You come from dust,
and to dust you shall return.

1523
01:38:18.309 --> 01:38:21.663
You come from dust,
and to dust you shall return.

1524
01:38:21.687 --> 01:38:25.525
Five hundred thousand!

1525
01:38:28.069 --> 01:38:34.117
You come from dust,
and to dust you shall return.

1526
01:38:37.036 --> 01:38:39.196
All I am saying is that be it LIG...
or an apartment...

1527
01:38:40.748 --> 01:38:46.105
...we'll stay together only wherever we go.

1528
01:38:46.129 --> 01:38:48.297
Have you ever wondered

1529
01:38:48.631 --> 01:38:50.550
about this fragile body?

1530
01:38:51.050 --> 01:38:53.278
The Gurus shed light,

1531
01:38:53.302 --> 01:38:55.697
but you could never comprehend.

1532
01:38:55.721 --> 01:38:57.557
Start stop, start stop,

1533
01:38:58.057 --> 01:39:00.059
the rhythms of breath

1534
01:39:00.393 --> 01:39:04.355
And when it does stop, what would
you have lost, what would you have gained?

1535
01:39:05.648 --> 01:39:10.254
You come from dust,
and to dust you shall return.

1536
01:39:10.278 --> 01:39:15.217
You come from dust,
and to dust you shall return.

1537
01:39:15.241 --> 01:39:17.952
Dear friend...

1538
01:39:19.871 --> 01:39:23.016
You come from dust,
and to dust you shall return

1539
01:39:23.040 --> 01:39:24.709
Let Baankey talk.

1540
01:39:25.459 --> 01:39:27.146
That's the first property deed...

1541
01:39:27.170 --> 01:39:30.607
...and this is the second one,
after increased rent...

1542
01:39:30.631 --> 01:39:32.401
- ...these are the receipts.
- Okay.

1543
01:39:32.425 --> 01:39:34.302
Let's show all these papers to Baankey.

1544
01:39:34.552 --> 01:39:36.220
- Everyone's ready?
- Yes.

1545
01:39:36.512 --> 01:39:38.866
- And papers are in place?
- By when will they be here?

1546
01:39:38.890 --> 01:39:39.932
They'll be here... ok?

1547
01:39:41.434 --> 01:39:42.434
Ya... right here.

1548
01:39:45.646 --> 01:39:47.875
- This way sir.
- Sir, may I put up the board?

1549
01:39:47.899 --> 01:39:50.127
Once I'm done with
reading the notice, then.

1550
01:39:50.151 --> 01:39:52.278
I really look forward to this part
of my job...

1551
01:39:52.778 --> 01:39:54.464
- One of you cops come with me.
- Ok sir.

1552
01:39:54.488 --> 01:39:55.740
This way sir...

1553
01:39:56.199 --> 01:39:58.409
Those guys are here, Baankey.

1554
01:39:59.493 --> 01:40:02.163
This way sir.

1555
01:40:02.496 --> 01:40:04.207
Mom... they are here...

1556
01:40:07.960 --> 01:40:10.731
- Do you see this place, sir?
- Hello.

1557
01:40:10.755 --> 01:40:12.798
I'm presuming everyone is here... come...

1558
01:40:13.216 --> 01:40:15.218
Yeah we're all here...
and ready...

1559
01:40:15.551 --> 01:40:16.886
Come, let's go.

1560
01:40:18.262 --> 01:40:21.241
MIRZA CHUNNAN NAWAB, are you...?

1561
01:40:21.265 --> 01:40:23.076
As if you didn't know my name.

1562
01:40:23.100 --> 01:40:24.100
Give me the notice.

1563
01:40:29.232 --> 01:40:30.650
Pay attention here.

1564
01:40:30.942 --> 01:40:32.068
This is an official notice.

1565
01:40:33.653 --> 01:40:38.383
After using and completing various
scientific methods of investigations...

1566
01:40:38.407 --> 01:40:40.427
...we, the archaeology department,
have come to a conclusion...

1567
01:40:40.451 --> 01:40:42.596
...that this 100 year
old mansion is not only...

1568
01:40:42.620 --> 01:40:44.500
...dangerous for the
habitants of this place...

1569
01:40:44.872 --> 01:40:51.379
...but is of an extreme
historical importance as well.

1570
01:40:51.879 --> 01:40:55.067
Therefore keeping in mind its possible
social and cultural contribution...

1571
01:40:55.091 --> 01:41:03.057
...we hereby declare that all the tenants
vacate this mansion at the earliest.

1572
01:41:03.307 --> 01:41:04.907
- By order.
- What is he saying, Baankey?

1573
01:41:05.142 --> 01:41:07.061
We have to leave? Where will we go?

1574
01:41:09.605 --> 01:41:11.375
What about our rights?

1575
01:41:11.399 --> 01:41:15.987
Wait I am asking... wait...
can you guys... shut up... I am talking!

1576
01:41:16.320 --> 01:41:18.715
Mr.Shukla, I went around
the whole town with you, for this?

1577
01:41:18.739 --> 01:41:19.859
Is this how you pay us back?

1578
01:41:20.032 --> 01:41:22.152
What about the LIG-MIG
apartments you had promised us?

1579
01:41:22.368 --> 01:41:23.553
Or was it part of your deceit plan?

1580
01:41:23.577 --> 01:41:26.098
Hand over the official notice to him
and put up the board outside.

1581
01:41:26.122 --> 01:41:27.307
I've no interest in this drama.

1582
01:41:27.331 --> 01:41:28.226
Drama?

1583
01:41:28.250 --> 01:41:29.542
Is this drama?

1584
01:41:30.251 --> 01:41:34.898
What the hell are you saying?

1585
01:41:34.922 --> 01:41:37.442
Shut up all of you.

1586
01:41:37.466 --> 01:41:39.306
You committed for LIG
MIG accommodation for us.

1587
01:41:39.802 --> 01:41:41.345
Why is it missing in the notice?

1588
01:41:41.971 --> 01:41:43.740
Why isn't it mentioned here?
We want it in writing.

1589
01:41:43.764 --> 01:41:46.034
Where do you reckon we'll go from here?
And what about this Mirza?

1590
01:41:46.058 --> 01:41:48.185
Why would he go anywhere...
he's the owner...

1591
01:41:48.477 --> 01:41:52.273
I get it... he's the owner so he stays...
And we're thrown out...

1592
01:41:53.024 --> 01:41:57.236
...and we...we are the doofus dogs
who fell for the bone you showed us...

1593
01:41:57.737 --> 01:41:59.756
...if I could throttle you just now.

1594
01:41:59.780 --> 01:42:02.509
You can't deny us those LIGs.

1595
01:42:02.533 --> 01:42:03.617
Put that stick away.

1596
01:42:03.909 --> 01:42:06.930
LIG comes under another department...
not mine...

1597
01:42:06.954 --> 01:42:08.515
But you never mentioned that earlier.

1598
01:42:08.539 --> 01:42:10.392
It's not as if we're
asking you to vacate now.

1599
01:42:10.416 --> 01:42:11.727
2 months notice is a good period.

1600
01:42:11.751 --> 01:42:15.439
Not good enough to find
a new accommodation!

1601
01:42:15.463 --> 01:42:19.800
No no... these pests can not
infest my mansion anymore...

1602
01:42:20.051 --> 01:42:22.678
And you guys leave too.

1603
01:42:22.928 --> 01:42:25.574
I've already sold off this mansion to
Mun Mun ji builders... so go...

1604
01:42:25.598 --> 01:42:28.035
And Christopher made it
all happen... now do you get it...?

1605
01:42:28.059 --> 01:42:29.119
We'll get a flat.

1606
01:42:29.143 --> 01:42:31.913
How can you sell it...?
It's utter rubbish...

1607
01:42:31.937 --> 01:42:34.273
Say what you may...
this place is sold!

1608
01:42:38.277 --> 01:42:39.570
Salute, sir.

1609
01:42:45.409 --> 01:42:47.596
We have thoroughly researched
this property, we are entitled...

1610
01:42:47.620 --> 01:42:50.790
Hey move... give way...
Mun Mun ji is here...

1611
01:42:51.082 --> 01:42:52.762
- Sir this way.
- Ah good job, Christopher.

1612
01:42:52.875 --> 01:42:54.418
- We'll have a garden here.
- Ok.

1613
01:42:54.752 --> 01:42:56.545
- And parking up to 3 floors.
- Very nice.

1614
01:42:57.046 --> 01:42:59.024
- You've really done superb this time around.
- Thank you.

1615
01:42:59.048 --> 01:43:02.218
- We can build up to 25 floors at least.
- Hold on... hold on.

1616
01:43:03.052 --> 01:43:04.678
You can't construct any building here.

1617
01:43:05.054 --> 01:43:06.531
This mansion is getting sealed.

1618
01:43:06.555 --> 01:43:09.201
- They are from archaeology department.
- Yeah that's ok you can seal it for now...

1619
01:43:09.225 --> 01:43:11.745
...once our cranes and bulldozer arrive,
we'll remove that seal.

1620
01:43:12.061 --> 01:43:13.997
- Sinha sir.
- You guys are not getting it...

1621
01:43:14.021 --> 01:43:17.417
...you can not construct a building
here, neither now nor in the future...

1622
01:43:17.441 --> 01:43:19.294
...we will be locking the gates.

1623
01:43:19.318 --> 01:43:20.921
Yes that's a good idea.

1624
01:43:20.945 --> 01:43:23.048
Christopher, once they put the locks,
take the keys from them.

1625
01:43:23.072 --> 01:43:24.091
Sure sir.

1626
01:43:24.115 --> 01:43:26.117
Yes mummy, I'll get the peas.

1627
01:43:35.334 --> 01:43:37.020
Take a picture for the records.

1628
01:43:37.044 --> 01:43:38.337
- I am Mirza!
- Click!

1629
01:43:39.880 --> 01:43:41.942
What is going on?!

1630
01:43:41.966 --> 01:43:43.050
Move away.

1631
01:43:43.426 --> 01:43:45.487
- What is going on...?
- Who's he?

1632
01:43:45.511 --> 01:43:48.073
- Existing Tenant...
- Tenant?!

1633
01:43:48.097 --> 01:43:50.409
Accountant, give him some cash.

1634
01:43:50.433 --> 01:43:51.433
Ok sir.

1635
01:43:51.475 --> 01:43:52.786
Give them a few bundles.

1636
01:43:52.810 --> 01:43:54.204
Oh yes... this we deserve.

1637
01:43:54.228 --> 01:43:55.997
- Please come in line.
- Just buy them out...

1638
01:43:56.021 --> 01:43:57.582
This is ours... not charity.

1639
01:43:57.606 --> 01:43:59.543
Why are you paying them...
this money is mine.

1640
01:43:59.567 --> 01:44:00.651
It's ours.

1641
01:44:06.449 --> 01:44:08.760
Look at this hyena... stealing my money.

1642
01:44:08.784 --> 01:44:11.495
I sold the mansion... my money.

1643
01:44:11.745 --> 01:44:12.788
How is it yours?!

1644
01:44:15.624 --> 01:44:16.876
Begum left us.

1645
01:44:17.793 --> 01:44:19.086
She's gone.

1646
01:44:21.046 --> 01:44:22.256
Begum's Gone!

1647
01:44:35.478 --> 01:44:36.896
What, what happened to her?

1648
01:44:38.772 --> 01:44:39.940
Begum's dead?

1649
01:44:40.441 --> 01:44:42.526
Who's Begum now?

1650
01:44:43.194 --> 01:44:44.914
Fatima Begum...
the owner of this mansion...

1651
01:44:45.571 --> 01:44:46.780
She's dead... so now?

1652
01:44:47.907 --> 01:44:49.033
It had to happen one day.

1653
01:44:49.283 --> 01:44:52.012
Now? Papers...?
Of this mansion?

1654
01:44:52.036 --> 01:44:53.078
All that must be in place.

1655
01:44:53.662 --> 01:44:55.039
We'll get them now.

1656
01:44:59.627 --> 01:45:02.087
Begum's gone... as in...?

1657
01:45:02.588 --> 01:45:08.219
As in gone... she's gone... Forever...

1658
01:45:09.011 --> 01:45:10.030
When...?

1659
01:45:10.054 --> 01:45:12.139
Three days back...
right in middle of the night.

1660
01:45:12.431 --> 01:45:13.599
Why didn't you tell me then?

1661
01:45:13.891 --> 01:45:16.435
Telling you now...
following her command.

1662
01:45:17.603 --> 01:45:18.771
Look there...

1663
01:45:35.162 --> 01:45:36.389
What happened, Baankey?

1664
01:45:36.413 --> 01:45:38.082
Tell us what's going on!

1665
01:45:46.799 --> 01:45:47.883
She's gone.

1666
01:45:51.679 --> 01:45:54.807
Is that her will?

1667
01:45:55.140 --> 01:45:58.018
Yes... her will.

1668
01:45:59.895 --> 01:46:01.063
Dear Mirza...

1669
01:46:01.564 --> 01:46:05.401
By the time you get this letter,
I'd be gone... far away.

1670
01:46:05.859 --> 01:46:08.255
Along with the actual documents...

1671
01:46:08.279 --> 01:46:11.448
...I've sold this mansion to Abdul
Rehman for a sum total of one rupee.

1672
01:46:11.949 --> 01:46:13.784
And will be with him, now on.

1673
01:46:15.202 --> 01:46:17.788
Sold off the mansion... as in...?

1674
01:46:18.163 --> 01:46:21.625
Begum isn't dead...
she has eloped.

1675
01:46:21.959 --> 01:46:23.061
What...?

1676
01:46:23.085 --> 01:46:25.129
Begum has eloped... she isn't dead.

1677
01:46:25.379 --> 01:46:26.422
What happened, Baankey?

1678
01:46:27.214 --> 01:46:28.233
What's wrong with Begum?

1679
01:46:28.257 --> 01:46:33.154
Begum is alive and has
eloped with her old lover.

1680
01:46:33.178 --> 01:46:34.656
- Eloped?
- Really?

1681
01:46:34.680 --> 01:46:36.807
With Abdul Rehman...

1682
01:46:39.101 --> 01:46:40.144
Begum?!

1683
01:46:40.436 --> 01:46:41.645
Mrs. Mishra! someone help...

1684
01:46:41.937 --> 01:46:43.230
Eloped... at this age?

1685
01:46:56.327 --> 01:46:57.967
What now, Shukla...?
Where will we go now?

1686
01:46:59.997 --> 01:47:01.433
Let's have a cup of tea.

1687
01:47:01.457 --> 01:47:02.541
Tea?

1688
01:47:03.000 --> 01:47:04.168
- Christopher.
- Sir!

1689
01:47:05.419 --> 01:47:09.048
One rupee!
You're offering a stash of money.

1690
01:47:09.423 --> 01:47:11.109
- I want this Abdul Rehman.
- Sure sir.

1691
01:47:11.133 --> 01:47:12.217
I knew it all along.

1692
01:47:13.260 --> 01:47:16.555
Good on her... wolves like you all
need to be treated this way.

1693
01:47:18.432 --> 01:47:20.142
Ruined... forever!

1694
01:47:29.443 --> 01:47:32.339
That day when you kept
inquiring about my family...

1695
01:47:32.363 --> 01:47:35.240
...you reminded me of the love
Abdul Rehman had for me.

1696
01:47:36.950 --> 01:47:39.190
While I always had an inkling
of your malicious intent...

1697
01:47:39.870 --> 01:47:44.333
...that day I became certain that you
wanted to nab my grand father's property...

1698
01:47:45.084 --> 01:47:47.461
...and were just waiting for me to die.

1699
01:47:50.047 --> 01:47:53.884
I broke Abdul Rehman's heart
and married you...

1700
01:47:54.551 --> 01:47:58.013
...because of my love
for this mansion...

1701
01:47:59.056 --> 01:48:00.408
...for I was born here.

1702
01:48:00.432 --> 01:48:03.161
On one side he wanted me to leave
all this and go to London with him...

1703
01:48:03.185 --> 01:48:05.497
...and here you,
you were ready to be a house husband.

1704
01:48:05.521 --> 01:48:09.108
This mansion was my weakness.

1705
01:48:10.025 --> 01:48:11.545
So I put my trust on you... my mistake

1706
01:48:12.361 --> 01:48:15.882
I knew all along that you were
responsible for all the petty thefts.

1707
01:48:15.906 --> 01:48:19.326
But I never interfered because
our house expenses were taken care of.

1708
01:48:29.044 --> 01:48:30.754
Move aside.

1709
01:48:35.092 --> 01:48:37.136
I am getting the gas cylinder...

1710
01:48:39.680 --> 01:48:40.973
We're taking it to the van...

1711
01:48:41.682 --> 01:48:42.992
Take this as well...

1712
01:48:43.016 --> 01:48:44.435
I'll take it, keep it here...

1713
01:48:56.989 --> 01:48:58.282
Let's go...

1714
01:49:37.446 --> 01:49:40.866
Well I always imagined that after me,
it'll be you who'll acquire this mansion...

1715
01:49:41.325 --> 01:49:44.369
...but when I realized that
you wanted to sell off the mansion...

1716
01:49:45.037 --> 01:49:47.414
...I decided to take
matters in my hand...

1717
01:49:47.915 --> 01:49:48.933
...and sold off the place.

1718
01:49:48.957 --> 01:49:49.997
May god be by your side...

1719
01:49:50.209 --> 01:49:53.337
Please do not touch anything...
it's all sold.

1720
01:49:57.216 --> 01:49:58.926
Though you aren't a bad man at heart...

1721
01:49:59.301 --> 01:50:03.472
...but no one can say when
the devil inside may take over...

1722
01:50:04.556 --> 01:50:09.686
...therefore all the legal proceedings
will be done by my lawyer...

1723
01:50:10.062 --> 01:50:12.481
...whom you may have seen
earlier as my doctor.

1724
01:50:14.233 --> 01:50:18.487
Now I am at ease that my mansion
will remain as is... untouched...

1725
01:50:20.906 --> 01:50:24.451
Shall we?...I need to put the locks...

